\ cross-cv8.4 - the CV8 cross compiler: kernel.4 and a design's overlays
\ compiled straight into the design's CV8 image, by a CV8 system - each
\ winning design rebuilds its own image (results/drafts/selfhost-plan-
\ 666.md). Until now every CV8 image was translated from a cell image by
\ tools/layout.py after RelF's cell engine ran it; relf's own cross.4 left
\ that path the same way in relf's Iteration 243.
\
\ A design is its genes: the words of a genes file (designs/NAME/genes.4,
\ written by lab/evolve/export-genes.py from what the evolver hands the
\ translator) - its overlays, fold set, specialisations, fused pairs,
\ format-10 operations, header and dictionary options. This file reads
\ them and does what the translator did, as it compiles: each definition
\ is a list of operations until its ; and then the design's rewrites run
\ over it in the translator's order, and it is laid out and encoded.
\ Run on a CV8 system, as the kernel workload runs cross.4:
\     S" extend.4" INCLUDED  S" genes.4" INCLUDED  S" cross-cv8.4" INCLUDED
\ and it writes cv8-self.img - and, for a design with the JIT, cv8-self-
\ jit.h: the image's layout as the JIT engine knows it (PART 9), for the
\ engine built to run it. Parts 1 and 2 are forth/cross.4's.
\ Based on SOD32 by L.C. Benschop and on RelF's cross.4.
\ Copyright 2001 - 2005, Kirill Timofeev, kt97679@gmail.com
\ The program is released under the GNU General Public License version 2.
\ There is NO WARRANTY.

\ Target cell width in bytes: the genes' G-CELL - 8, or 4 for a 32-bit
\ target (forth/cross.4's one line).
\ 723: gene constants an older genes.4 lacks (0 there) - so the ten designs' genes need no export for them.
CREATE GENE-BUF 32 ALLOT
: GENE? ( c-addr u --- n ) GENE-BUF PLACE GENE-BUF FIND IF EXECUTE ELSE DROP 0 THEN ;
S" G-JITDEAD" GENE? CONSTANT X-JITDEAD   \ the gene jitdead (layout.py --jit-dead)
S" G-JITX" GENE? CONSTANT X-JITX         \ --jitx

VARIABLE TARGET-CELL-BYTES
G-CELL TARGET-CELL-BYTES !

\ PART 1: THE VOCABULARIES.

VOCABULARY TARGET
\ This vocabulary will hold shadow definitions for all words that are in
\ the target dictionary. When a shadow definition is executed, it
\ performs the compile action in the target dictionary.

VOCABULARY TRANSIENT
\ This vocabulary will hold definitions that must be executed by the
\ host system ( the system on which the cross compiler runs) and that
\ compile to the target system.

\ Expl: The word IF occurs in all three vocabularies. The word IF in the
\       FORTH vocabulary is run by the host system and is used when
\       compiling host definitions. A different version is in the
\       TRANSIENT vocabulary. This one runs on the host system and
\       is used when compiling target definitions. The version in the
\       TARGET vocabulary is the version that will run on the target
\       system.


\ PART 2: THE TARGET DICTIONARY SPACE.

\ Next we need to define the target space and the words to access it.

40000 CONSTANT IMAGE_SIZE

CREATE IMAGE IMAGE_SIZE CHARS ALLOT \ This space contains the target image.
       IMAGE IMAGE_SIZE 0 FILL      \ Initialize it to zero.

\ Fetch and store characters in the target space.
: C@-T ( t-addr --- c) CHARS IMAGE + C@ ;
: C!-T ( c t-addr ---) CHARS IMAGE + C! ;

\ Fetch and store cells in the target space, TARGET-CELL-BYTES wide.
\ As of phase 5 (see GOALS.md), images are native host endianness, not a
\ portable on-disk format. These build/take apart a little-endian value
\ byte by byte via C@-T/C!-T (not plain @/! on this host), because
\ that's what makes the *disk file* end up in the intended byte order:
\ WRITE-FILE (on whatever engine happens to be running this) reverses
\ whatever it writes, and C@-T/C!-T's own byte-level access already
\ cancels that reversal out (see PROGRESS.md for the derivation) - the
\ same reason name strings/PLACE-T never needed any special handling
\ either. Safe on this host regardless of TARGET-CELL-BYTES: this host's
\ own cells are always at least as wide as the target's (see PROGRESS.md,
\ phase 2, for what goes wrong when that's not true, and why building a
\ *narrower* target from a wider host - unlike phase 2's situation - has
\ no equivalent problem).
\ BEGIN/WHILE/REPEAT with an explicit counter, not DO/LOOP: DO/LOOP here
\ reliably hung the bootstrap somewhere past kernel.4 loading (found by
\ bisection, not fully root-caused - see PROGRESS.md). These are called
\ often enough, from enough different contexts, that avoiding DO/LOOP's
\ own return-stack usage entirely was the safer fix.
: @-T  ( t-addr --- x)
  0 0
  BEGIN
    DUP TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ <
  WHILE
    >R OVER R@ CHARS + C@-T R@ 3 LSHIFT LSHIFT OR R> 1+
  REPEAT
  DROP SWAP DROP
  \ Sign-extend when the target cell is narrower than this host's own
  \ (this host's cells are always at least as wide as the target's, see
  \ the note on C@-T/C!-T above): the loop above only fills the low
  \ TARGET-CELL-BYTES bytes, leaving the high bytes zero regardless of
  \ the target value's actual sign. Negative target-level sentinels
  \ (FORWARD's own -1, used by RESOLVE's chain-termination check) need
  \ those high bytes properly extended to compare correctly against
  \ host -1 - otherwise RESOLVE's BEGIN/WHILE loop never sees them as
  \ equal and walks off the end of the chain into unrelated memory.
  \ Iteration 328: narrower than this host's own, as said - it read "8 <", a 64-bit host
  \ taken for granted: on a 32-bit host building the 4-byte kernel it extended anyway, and
  \ -1 32 LSHIFT on a 4-byte cell is a full-width shift (x86 masks it to 0, -1 is left):
  \ every negative link became -1, and POSTPONE's thread walk crashed. [ 1 CELLS ] LITERAL
  \ compiles the very literal 8 did on a 64-bit host.
  TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ [ 1 CELLS ] LITERAL < IF
    DUP 1 TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ 3 LSHIFT 1 - LSHIFT AND IF
      -1 TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ 3 LSHIFT LSHIFT OR
    THEN
  THEN ;
: !-T  ( x t-addr ---)
  0
  BEGIN
    DUP TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ <
  WHILE
    >R OVER R@ 3 LSHIFT RSHIFT OVER R@ CHARS + C!-T R> 1+
  REPEAT
  DROP 2DROP ;

\ A dictionary is constructed in the target space. Here are the primitives
\ to maintain the dictionary pointer and to reserve space.

VARIABLE DP-T                       \ Dictionary pointer for target dictionary.
0 DP-T !                            \ Initialize it to zero, SOD starts at 0.
: THERE ( --- t-addr) DP-T @ ;      \ Equivalent of HERE in target space.
: ALLOT-T ( n --- ) DP-T +! ;       \ Reserve n bytes in the dictionary.
: CHARS-T ( n1 --- n2 ) ;
: CELLS-T ( n1 --- n2 ) TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ * ;  \ n1 target cells in bytes.
: ALIGN-T                           \ Target only accesses cells at aligned
                                    \ addresses.
  BEGIN THERE TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ 1- AND WHILE 1 ALLOT-T REPEAT ;
: ALIGNED-T ( n1 --- n2 )
  TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ 1- + TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ NEGATE AND ;
: C,-T  ( c --- )  THERE C!-T 1 CHARS ALLOT-T ;
: ,-T   ( x --- )  THERE !-T  1 CELLS-T ALLOT-T ;

: PLACE-T ( c-addr len t-addr --- ) \ Move counted string to target space.
  OVER OVER C!-T 1+ CHARS IMAGE + SWAP CHARS CMOVE ;


\ PART 3: HEADERS - byte-granular, as forth/cv8b.4's HEADER8 lays them:
\     [link: 1-4 bytes, tag byte last][count][name][body]
\ The link is the distance back from this word's count byte to the
\ previous one in its thread, 0 at a thread's end. The engine never
\ reads a link; the target's SEARCH-WORDLIST does.

VARIABLE TLINK 0 TLINK !   \ The count byte of the last header, 0 if it had none.

\ The target's word list is HASHED (kernel.4's FORTH-WORDLIST) into the
\ design's G-THREADS chains, threaded exactly as the target searches it.
G-THREADS CONSTANT #TTHREADS
CREATE TTHREADS #TTHREADS CELLS ALLOT
TTHREADS #TTHREADS CELLS 0 FILL

: THASH ( c-addr u --- n )
\ Exactly what kernel.4's HASH produces for the same name and count - and,
\ with G-HASHK (Iteration 731), cv8-hashk.4's HASH8: v times K, its middle bits.
  #TTHREADS >R
  OVER C@ 1 LSHIFT OVER 1 > IF ROT 1+ C@ 2 LSHIFT XOR ELSE ROT DROP
   THEN XOR
  G-HASHK ?DUP IF * 8 RSHIFT THEN
  R> 1- AND ;

: PUBLISH-WORDLIST ( t-addr --- )
\ The thread heads into the target's word list: cell 0 the count, then
\ the heads.
  DUP #TTHREADS SWAP !-T
  #TTHREADS 0 DO
    I CELLS TTHREADS + @
    OVER I 1+ CELLS-T + !-T
  LOOP
  DROP ;

VARIABLE THIS-THREAD
VARIABLE HEAD-T
VARIABLE HLEN-T

: LINK-LEN-T ( d --- n )
  G-TAG2 IF
    DUP 64 U< IF DROP 1 EXIT THEN
    DUP 16384 U< IF DROP 2 EXIT THEN
    4194304 U< IF 3 ELSE 4 THEN EXIT
  THEN
  DUP 128 U< IF DROP 1 EXIT THEN
  DUP 16384 U< IF DROP 2 EXIT THEN
  2097152 U< IF 3 ELSE 4 THEN ;

: LINK,-T ( d n --- )
\ A link of exactly n bytes, its tag byte last (cv8b.4's LINK,); under
\ the two-bit tag the low bytes first and the tag, n - 1, in the top two
\ bits of the last (cv8bt.4's LINK,).
  G-TAG2 IF
    1- DUP >R BEGIN DUP WHILE >R DUP 255 AND C,-T 8 RSHIFT R> 1- REPEAT DROP R> 6 LSHIFT OR C,-T EXIT
  THEN
  DUP 1 = IF DROP C,-T EXIT THEN
  DUP 2 = IF DROP DUP 255 AND C,-T 8 RSHIFT 128 OR C,-T EXIT THEN
  DUP 3 = IF DROP DUP 255 AND C,-T DUP 8 RSHIFT 255 AND C,-T
    16 RSHIFT 192 OR C,-T EXIT THEN
  DROP DUP 255 AND C,-T DUP 8 RSHIFT 255 AND C,-T DUP 16 RSHIFT 255 AND C,-T
  24 RSHIFT 224 OR C,-T ;

\ Lists of names, each followed by one space, searched by place; the
\ genes are such lists.
VARIABLE LA  VARIABLE LU  VARIABLE LI
: LIST-STEP ( --- len ) 0 BEGIN DUP LA @ + C@ 32 = 0= WHILE 1+ REPEAT ;
: LIST-NEXT ( len --- ) 1+ DUP LA +! NEGATE LU +! 1 LI +! ;
: LIST-INDEX ( c-addr u list-a list-u --- i | -1 )
  LU ! LA ! 0 LI !
  BEGIN LU @ WHILE
    LIST-STEP >R 2DUP LA @ R@ COMPARE 0= IF 2DROP R> DROP LI @ EXIT THEN
    R> LIST-NEXT
  REPEAT 2DROP -1 ;
: LIST-TOKEN ( k list-a list-u --- c-addr u )
  LU ! LA ! 0 LI !
  BEGIN DUP LI @ = 0= WHILE LIST-STEP LIST-NEXT REPEAT DROP LA @ LIST-STEP ;
: LIST-COUNT ( list-a list-u --- n )
  LU ! LA ! 0 LI ! BEGIN LU @ WHILE LIST-STEP LIST-NEXT REPEAT LI @ ;
: TOKEN>N ( c-addr u --- n ) >R >R 0 0 R> R> >NUMBER 2DROP DROP ;
: LIST-VALUE ( c-addr u list-a list-u --- n | -1 )
\ In a list of name-number pairs, the number after this name, or -1.
  2DUP >R >R LIST-INDEX DUP 0< IF R> R> 2DROP EXIT THEN
  DUP 1 AND IF DROP R> R> 2DROP -1 EXIT THEN
  1+ R> R> LIST-TOKEN TOKEN>N ;

\ chainorder (Iteration 736; tools/layout.py --chainorder, forth/cv8-chainorder.4): each chain starts with its most
\ looked-up names (G-CO-HOT: name and count - lab/evolve/chainorder-use.txt's, at least --chainorder-min), most first,
\ the rest newest first as before. Every pass logs its headers; the second pass's give the walk (CO-WALK!), and the
\ third lays each link to the next header of its chain's walk - back sized as NAME,-T sizes one, forward three bytes in
\ their own form (the tag F0-FF; under the two-bit tag E0-FF), patched when the headers are all down (CO-FINISH).
4096 CONSTANT #HDR-MAX
CREATE HDR-TH   #HDR-MAX CELLS ALLOT   \ each header's chain
CREATE HDR-RANK #HDR-MAX CELLS ALLOT   \ its name's count in G-CO-HOT, 0 not hot
CREATE HDR-NFA  #HDR-MAX CELLS ALLOT   \ its count byte's place
CREATE HDR-SUM  #HDR-MAX CELLS ALLOT   \ its name, summed: the passes must lay the same headers
CREATE HDR-PSUM #HDR-MAX CELLS ALLOT   \ ...the pass before's
CREATE HDR-NEXT #HDR-MAX CELLS ALLOT   \ the walk's next header, -1 none (from the pass before)
CREATE CO-HEAD #TTHREADS CELLS ALLOT   \ each chain's first header in the walk, -1 none
CREATE CO-FWD #HDR-MAX 2 * CELLS ALLOT \ forward links to patch: the site, the header it reaches
CREATE PICKED #HDR-MAX ALLOT
VARIABLE #HDR  VARIABLE #HDR-PREV  VARIABLE #CO-FWD  VARIABLE CO-WALK  VARIABLE CO-TH  VARIABLE CO-PREV
0 #HDR !  0 #HDR-PREV !  0 #CO-FWD !  0 CO-WALK !
: NAME-SUM ( c-addr u --- n ) 0 ROT ROT OVER + SWAP ?DO 31 * I C@ + LOOP ;
: CO-LOG ( c-addr u --- )
\ The header just laid, THERE its count byte's place.
  #HDR @ #HDR-MAX < 0= ABORT" cross: chainorder - too many headers"
  2DUP NAME-SUM #HDR @ CELLS HDR-SUM + !
  G-CO-HOT LIST-VALUE 0 MAX #HDR @ CELLS HDR-RANK + !
  THIS-THREAD @ #HDR @ CELLS HDR-TH + !
  THERE #HDR @ CELLS HDR-NFA + !  1 #HDR +! ;
: CO-LINK, ( c-addr u --- )
\ The link of this pass's header #HDR: to the next of its chain's walk.
  #HDR @ #HDR-PREV @ < 0= ABORT" cross: chainorder - more headers than the pass before"
  NAME-SUM #HDR @ CELLS HDR-PSUM + @ <> ABORT" cross: chainorder - the headers moved between passes"
  #HDR @ CELLS HDR-NEXT + @
  DUP 0< IF DROP 0 1 LINK,-T EXIT THEN
  DUP #HDR @ < IF                                     \ back: laid already, sized as NAME,-T sizes it
    CELLS HDR-NFA + @ >R
    THERE G-TAG2 IF 4 ELSE 3 THEN + R@ - LINK-LEN-T
    THERE OVER + R> - SWAP LINK,-T EXIT
  THEN
  THERE #CO-FWD @ 2 * CELLS CO-FWD + !  #CO-FWD @ 2 * 1+ CELLS CO-FWD + !  1 #CO-FWD +!
  0 C,-T 0 C,-T 0 C,-T ;                              \ forward: patched by CO-FINISH
: CO-BETTER? ( k best --- f )
\ k before best in the walk: a higher count, or as high and newer (k later - the log is in order).
  DUP 0< IF 2DROP -1 EXIT THEN
  CELLS HDR-RANK + @ SWAP CELLS HDR-RANK + @ SWAP < 0= ;
: CO-PICK ( --- k | -1 )
  -1 #HDR @ 0 ?DO
    I CELLS HDR-TH + @ CO-TH @ = I PICKED + C@ 0= AND IF I OVER CO-BETTER? IF DROP I THEN THEN
  LOOP ;
: CO-WALK! ( --- )
\ Each chain's walk from this pass's log, for the next pass.
  #HDR @ 0 ?DO -1 I CELLS HDR-NEXT + ! LOOP
  PICKED #HDR-MAX 0 FILL
  #TTHREADS 0 DO
    I CO-TH !  -1 I CELLS CO-HEAD + !  -1 CO-PREV !
    BEGIN CO-PICK DUP 0< 0= WHILE
      1 OVER PICKED + C!
      CO-PREV @ 0< IF DUP CO-TH @ CELLS CO-HEAD + ! ELSE DUP CO-PREV @ CELLS HDR-NEXT + ! THEN
      CO-PREV !
    REPEAT DROP
  LOOP
  HDR-SUM HDR-PSUM #HDR @ CELLS CMOVE  #HDR @ #HDR-PREV ! ;
: CO-FINISH ( --- )
\ The walk's pass, its headers down: the forward links patched, each chain's head its walk's first.
  #HDR @ #HDR-PREV @ <> ABORT" cross: chainorder - fewer headers than the pass before"
  #CO-FWD @ 0 ?DO
    I 2 * CELLS CO-FWD + @  I 2 * 1+ CELLS CO-FWD + @ CELLS HDR-NFA + @   ( site target )
    OVER 3 + -                                        ( site e )  \ from this header's count byte, site + 3
    DUP G-TAG2 IF 2097152 ELSE 1048576 THEN U< 0= ABORT" cross: a forward link out of reach"
    2DUP 255 AND SWAP C!-T  2DUP 8 RSHIFT 255 AND SWAP 1+ C!-T
    16 RSHIFT G-TAG2 IF 224 ELSE 240 THEN OR SWAP 2 + C!-T
  LOOP
  #TTHREADS 0 DO I CELLS CO-HEAD + @ DUP 0< IF DROP 0 ELSE CELLS HDR-NFA + @ THEN I CELLS TTHREADS + ! LOOP ;

: NAME,-T ( c-addr u --- )
\ The header for a name, linked as HEADER8 links one at run time: the
\ link sized for the farthest its count byte can land, THERE + 3. With
\ chainorder's walk (the third pass), to the next header of its walk.
  DUP 31 > ABORT" cross: name too long"
  2DUP THASH THIS-THREAD !
  G-CHAINORDER CO-WALK @ AND IF 2DUP CO-LINK, ELSE
  THIS-THREAD @ CELLS TTHREADS + @ HEAD-T !
  HEAD-T @ IF THERE G-TAG2 IF 4 ELSE 3 THEN + HEAD-T @ - LINK-LEN-T ELSE 1 THEN HLEN-T !
  HEAD-T @ IF THERE HLEN-T @ + HEAD-T @ - ELSE 0 THEN HLEN-T @ LINK,-T
  THEN
  G-CHAINORDER IF 2DUP CO-LOG THEN
  THERE TLINK !
  THERE THIS-THREAD @ CELLS TTHREADS + !
  DUP C,-T THERE CHARS IMAGE + SWAP DUP ALLOT-T CMOVE ;


\ Every target word has a shadow in TARGET. Its fields: [t-xt][kind]
\ [value: a primitive's opcode, a constant's value, or the opcode a call
\ to a colon word becomes][t-nfa][host action][immediate][test-branch
\ long opcode][...short opcode]. Executed, the shadow does what the
\ word's name means where the cross compiler meets it: inside a
\ definition it adds an operation; outside one, the host action - the
\ host word I-name, if there is one (I-! stores into the image) - or a
\ data word's parameter address, or a constant's value.
0 CONSTANT K-COLON
1 CONSTANT K-PRIM
2 CONSTANT K-DATA
3 CONSTANT K-CONST

' TARGET >BODY @ CONSTANT TARGET-WID

CREATE IBUF 40 ALLOT
: INTERP-XT ( c-addr u --- xt | 0 )
\ The host word I-name, or 0.
  DUP 2 + IBUF C! 73 IBUF 1+ C! 45 IBUF 2 + C!
  IBUF 3 + SWAP CMOVE
  IBUF COUNT FORTH-WORDLIST SEARCH-WORDLIST IF ELSE 0 THEN ;

: T-SHADOW ( c-addr u --- shadow-body -1 | 0 )
  TARGET-WID SEARCH-WORDLIST IF >BODY -1 ELSE 0 THEN ;

: T' ( "name" --- t-xt )
\ The execution token of a target word, by name.
  BL WORD COUNT T-SHADOW 0= ABORT" cross: no such target word" @ ;

: >BODY-T ( t-xt --- t-addr )
\ A data word's parameter field: [DOVAR][room for DOES>'s far call -
\ three bytes, four under the two-bit tag] and aligned - cv8b.4's and
\ cv8bt.4's >BODY8, CV8-DOES-RESERVE 3 or 4.
  G-TAG2 IF 5 ELSE 4 THEN + ALIGNED-T ;

: .TNAME ( t-nfa --- ) ?DUP IF DUP C@-T 31 AND SWAP 1+ CHARS IMAGE + SWAP TYPE ELSE ." (headerless)" THEN ;

\ PART 4: CODE GENERATION. A definition's code is a list of operations
\ until its ; - then the design's rewrites run over it, in the order the
\ translator ran them on a word (tools/sod16.py's read_ops: specialise,
\ format-10 operations, fold, pairs, test-branches, short branches), and
\ it is laid out and encoded. A rewrite takes two neighbours only where
\ nothing branches to the second: every branch's landing place is marked.

VARIABLE STATE-T 0 STATE-T ! \ State variable for cross compiler.
: T] 1 STATE-T ! ;
: T[ 0 STATE-T ! ;

VARIABLE CSP   \ Stack pointer checking between : and ;
: !CSP DEPTH CSP ! ;
: ?CSP DEPTH CSP @ - ABORT" Incomplete control structure" ;

: W,-T ( n --- ) DUP 255 AND C,-T 8 RSHIFT 255 AND C,-T ;
: 32,-T ( n --- ) DUP W,-T 16 RSHIFT W,-T ;
: W!-T ( n t-addr --- ) 2DUP C!-T 1+ SWAP 8 RSHIFT 255 AND SWAP C!-T ;

: CALLSIZE-T ( t-addr --- n )
\ A call's bytes: CV8 two below 16 KB, three below 2 MB (cv8.4's CALL,);
\ under the two-bit tag two, three below 4 MB (none with the wide form),
\ four (cv8t.4's CALL,).
  G-TAG2 IF
    DUP 16384 < IF DROP 2 EXIT THEN
    G-T2WIDE IF DROP 4 EXIT THEN
    4194304 < IF 3 ELSE 4 THEN EXIT
  THEN
  16384 < IF 2 ELSE 3 THEN ;
: CALLN,-T ( t-addr n --- )
\ A call of n bytes: the byte offset from the image base (call scale 0) -
\ CV8 10xxxxxx and 110xxxxx; the tag 01, 10, 11 in the top two bits and
\ the rest high byte first (FORMAT-TAG2.md).
  G-TAG2 IF
    2DUP 8 * 2 - 1 SWAP LSHIFT < 0= ABORT" cross: call beyond reach"
    2DUP 1- 8 * RSHIFT OVER 1- 6 LSHIFT OR C,-T
    1- BEGIN DUP WHILE 1- 2DUP 8 * RSHIFT 255 AND C,-T REPEAT 2DROP EXIT
  THEN
  2 = IF DUP 16384 < 0= ABORT" cross: call beyond reach" DUP 8 RSHIFT 128 OR C,-T 255 AND C,-T EXIT THEN
  DUP 2097152 < 0= ABORT" cross: call beyond reach"
  DUP 16 RSHIFT 192 OR C,-T DUP 8 RSHIFT 255 AND C,-T 255 AND C,-T ;
: CALL-BYTES-T ( t-addr --- ) DUP CALLSIZE-T CALLN,-T ;

: SLOTSIZE-T ( t-addr --- n ) G-VARSLOT IF 32768 < IF 2 ELSE 3 THEN ELSE DROP 2 THEN ;
: SLOT,-T ( t-addr --- )
\ A slot operand: the byte offset from the base (scale 0), high byte
\ first - 15 bits in 2 bytes, 23 in 3 with the top bit set (vm-lab.c's
\ SLOT()); an engine without VARSLOT reads two bytes, low first.
  G-VARSLOT 0= IF DUP 65536 < 0= ABORT" cross: slot beyond reach" DUP 255 AND C,-T 8 RSHIFT C,-T EXIT THEN
  DUP 32768 < IF DUP 8 RSHIFT C,-T 255 AND C,-T EXIT THEN
  DUP 8388608 < 0= ABORT" cross: slot beyond reach"
  DUP 16 RSHIFT 128 OR C,-T DUP 8 RSHIFT 255 AND C,-T 255 AND C,-T ;

\ ---- one operation, two formats (FORMAT-TAG2.md) --------------------------
\ An operation is its logical number - the translator's: kernel.4's
\ primitive order, compacted; an escaped primitive 256 + its selector;
\ LIT32 68, DOVAR 69 and the rest below. Its bytes are the format's: in
\ CV8 the number itself, an escaped primitive ESC (125) and its selector;
\ under the two-bit tag (G-TAG2) the design's code for it, from the
\ engine's own map (vm-tag2-one.h, vm-tag2-esc.h) - one byte, or the
\ escape 0x3F and a selector. (The map numbers an escaped primitive
\ 128 + its selector; the JIT's operation is 65533.)
CREATE T2ONE 256 ALLOT  T2ONE 256 0 FILL      \ logical number -> code + 1, or 0
CREATE T2ESC 256 ALLOT  T2ESC 256 0 FILL      \ ...-> escape selector + 1, or 0
VARIABLE T2JIT -1 T2JIT !                      \ the JIT's code
VARIABLE T2JITN -1 T2JITN !                    \ jitdead's JITN code (65532 in the map; Iteration 723)
: T2-LOAD ( --- )
  G-T2-ONE LIST-COUNT 2 / 0 ?DO
    I 2 * G-T2-ONE LIST-TOKEN TOKEN>N  I 2 * 1+ G-T2-ONE LIST-TOKEN TOKEN>N      ( L code )
    OVER 65533 = IF T2JIT ! DROP ELSE OVER 65532 = IF T2JITN ! DROP ELSE
    OVER 256 < 0= ABORT" cross: a map entry past 255" 1+ SWAP T2ONE + C! THEN THEN
  LOOP
  G-T2-ESC LIST-COUNT 2 / 0 ?DO
    I 2 * G-T2-ESC LIST-TOKEN TOKEN>N  I 2 * 1+ G-T2-ESC LIST-TOKEN TOKEN>N
    OVER 256 < 0= ABORT" cross: a map entry past 255" 1+ SWAP T2ESC + C!
  LOOP ;
T2-LOAD
: >L2 ( op --- L ) DUP 256 < IF EXIT THEN DUP 512 < IF 128 - THEN ;
: T2C ( op --- code | 0 )
\ A table's byte for an operation: its one-byte code, 0 for none or an
\ escaped one (layout.py: "0 means none, as the overlays read it").
  ?DUP 0= IF 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP 65533 = IF DROP T2JIT @ 0 MAX EXIT THEN
  >L2 DUP 256 < IF T2ONE + C@ DUP IF 1- THEN ELSE DROP 0 THEN ;
: OPSIZE-T ( op --- n )
  G-TAG2 IF
    DUP 65533 = IF DROP 1 EXIT THEN
    >L2 DUP 256 < 0= ABORT" cross: an operation past the map"
    DUP T2ONE + C@ IF DROP 1 EXIT THEN
    T2ESC + C@ 0= ABORT" cross: an operation the engine's map lacks" 2 EXIT
  THEN
  256 < IF 1 ELSE 2 THEN ;
: OP,-T ( op --- )
  G-TAG2 IF
    DUP 65533 = IF DROP T2JIT @ DUP 0< ABORT" cross: no JIT code in the map" C,-T EXIT THEN
    >L2 DUP 256 < 0= ABORT" cross: an operation past the map"
    DUP T2ONE + C@ ?DUP IF 1- C,-T DROP EXIT THEN
    T2ESC + C@ DUP 0= ABORT" cross: an operation the engine's map lacks" 63 C,-T 1- C,-T EXIT
  THEN
  DUP 256 < IF C,-T ELSE 125 C,-T 256 - C,-T THEN ;

\ ---- the design's opcodes ----------------------------------------------
\ Fixed in every CV8 engine: EXIT 1, BRANCH 3, ?BRANCH 4 (kernel.4's
\ order), LIT32 68, DOVAR 69, LIT8 71, LIT8X 72, LIT64 124; LIT16 is the
\ LIT primitive's. The rest is the design's: the fold set (FOLD-BASE +
\ place), its specialisations (0x60-0x7B), its pairs, its format-10
\ operations, its fused test-branches and short branches.
73 CONSTANT FOLD-BASE
CREATE FOLDMAP 128 ALLOT  FOLDMAP 128 0 FILL   \ opcode -> folded opcode, or 0
: SPEC? ( bit --- f ) G-SPEC AND 0= 0= ;

: SPECIAL-SET ( --- c-addr u ) S" + = @ ! DUP SWAP < " ;      \ the primitives the patterns name
CREATE SPECIAL-OPS 8 CELLS ALLOT  SPECIAL-OPS 8 CELLS -1 FILL
: SPECIAL ( i --- op ) CELLS SPECIAL-OPS + @ ;

: TINY-SET ( --- c-addr u )
  S" 0= - <> 0< > 2DUP 2DROP CHAR+ 1+ CELL+ CELLS 1- INVERT COUNT ALIGNED " ;
105 CONSTANT TINY-BASE

\ The fused test-branches: a test, then ?BRANCH (tools/sod16.py's TESTBR),
\ the long one's name; the short one's is it and 8.
: TEST-SET ( --- c-addr u )
  S" 0= ?NBRANCH < <?BRANCH = =?BRANCH U< U<?BRANCH - <>?BRANCH <> <>?BRANCH > >?BRANCH 0< 0<?BRANCH DUP DUP?BRANCH OVER OVER?BRANCH " ;
CREATE TBUF 40 ALLOT
: OPS10-OF ( c-addr u --- op | 0 ) G-OPS10 LIST-VALUE DUP 0< IF DROP 0 THEN ;
: BR8-OP ( --- op | 0 ) S" BRANCH8" OPS10-OF ;
: QBR8-OP ( --- op | 0 ) S" ?BRANCH8" OPS10-OF ;
: TEST-OPS ( c-addr u --- long short | 0 0 )
\ The fused test-branch opcodes for a word of this name, if the design
\ has them.
  2DUP TEST-SET LIST-INDEX DUP 0< IF DROP 2DROP 0 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP 1 AND IF DROP 2DROP 0 0 EXIT THEN
  >R 2DROP R> 1+ TEST-SET LIST-TOKEN               ( c-addr' u' )
  DUP >R TBUF SWAP CMOVE R>                        ( u' )
  TBUF OVER OPS10-OF DUP 0= IF 2DROP 0 0 EXIT THEN ( u' long )
  SWAP 56 OVER TBUF + C! TBUF SWAP 1+ OPS10-OF ;

\ ---- the operations of the definition being compiled -------------------
2048 CONSTANT #OPS-MAX
CREATE OPS #OPS-MAX 4 * CELLS ALLOT
CREATE TGTS #OPS-MAX 1+ ALLOT
CREATE ADDRS #OPS-MAX 1+ CELLS ALLOT
CREATE LONG #OPS-MAX ALLOT                      \ a branch that cannot take its short form
VARIABLE #OPS
CREATE SPOOL 8192 ALLOT  VARIABLE SPOOL#       \ the definition's strings

\ An operation: [kind][a][b][c].
0 CONSTANT O-DEAD    \ taken into the operation before it
1 CONSTANT O-P       \ a: opcode; c: the shadow (a word's own name), or 0
2 CONSTANT O-C       \ a: the callee's t-addr; c: its shadow
3 CONSTANT O-F       \ a: a FORWARD's body - a word called before it exists
4 CONSTANT O-LIT     \ a: the value
5 CONSTANT O-BR      \ a: the target operation; b: long opcode; c: short opcode or 0
6 CONSTANT O-DC      \ a: a data word's t-xt; b: its parameter field
7 CONSTANT O-LOOPC   \ a: a FORWARD's body; b: target operation - a call and the cell after it
8 CONSTANT O-PPC     \ a: (POSTPONE)'s FORWARD body; b: the xt - a call and the cell after it
9 CONSTANT O-STR     \ a: the string; b: its length - counted, then aligned
10 CONSTANT O-SLOT   \ a: VF or VS; b: the parameter field
11 CONSTANT O-IMM    \ a: ADDI, EQI or their X forms; b: n
12 CONSTANT O-LITX   \ a: the value - a literal and the EXIT after it
13 CONSTANT O-RB     \ a: a rebound name's record
16 CONSTANT O-EQBR   \ a: the target operation; b: n; c: the short opcode or 0 - EQI n ?BRANCH as =I?BRANCH (722)

: OP# ( i --- a-addr ) 4 * CELLS OPS + ;
: OP-K ( i --- k ) OP# @ ;
: OP-A ( i --- a ) OP# CELL+ @ ;
: OP-B ( i --- b ) OP# 2 CELLS + @ ;
: OP-C ( i --- c ) OP# 3 CELLS + @ ;
: OP! ( k a b c i --- ) OP# >R R@ 3 CELLS + ! R@ 2 CELLS + ! R@ CELL+ ! R> ! ;
: OP+ ( k a b c --- )
  #OPS @ #OPS-MAX 1- < 0= ABORT" cross: a definition too long"
  #OPS @ OP! 1 #OPS +! ;
: BR? ( i --- f ) OP-K DUP O-BR = SWAP O-EQBR = OR ;   \ 722: a branch - its a the target operation
: KILL ( i --- ) >R O-DEAD 0 0 0 R> OP! ;
: MARK ( i --- ) TGTS + 1 SWAP C! ;
: TGT? ( i --- f ) TGTS + C@ ;
: CODE-START ( --- ) 0 #OPS ! TGTS #OPS-MAX 1+ 0 FILL 0 SPOOL# ! ;

\ The dead operations out, after each rewrite, as the translator's lists
\ have none: each later one moves down, a branch's target and a loop's
\ start with it, and the landing marks. (Nothing that is landed on is
\ ever taken into the operation before it.)
CREATE NEWIDX #OPS-MAX 1+ CELLS ALLOT
CREATE TGTS2 #OPS-MAX 1+ ALLOT
: NEW# ( i --- j ) CELLS NEWIDX + @ ;
: COMPACT ( --- )
  0 #OPS @ 0 ?DO I CELLS NEWIDX + OVER SWAP ! I OP-K O-DEAD = 0= IF 1+ THEN LOOP
  #OPS @ CELLS NEWIDX + !
  TGTS2 #OPS-MAX 1+ 0 FILL
  #OPS @ 1+ 0 ?DO I TGT? IF 1 I NEW# TGTS2 + C! THEN LOOP
  #OPS @ 0 ?DO
    I OP-K O-DEAD = 0= IF
      I BR? IF I OP-A DUP 0< 0= IF NEW# THEN I OP# CELL+ ! THEN
      I OP-K O-LOOPC = IF I OP-B NEW# I OP# 2 CELLS + ! THEN
      I OP# I NEW# OP# 4 CELLS CMOVE
    THEN
  LOOP
  #OPS @ NEW# #OPS !
  TGTS2 TGTS #OPS-MAX 1+ CMOVE ;

: P+ ( op shadow --- ) >R O-P SWAP 0 R> OP+ ;
: T-NORM ( n --- n' )
\ A target cell's value as this host holds it - on a host wider than the
\ target, its low bytes sign-extended, as @-T reads a cell: -1 and
\ $FFFFFFFF are one literal for a 32-bit target, whichever host builds it.
  TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ [ 1 CELLS ] LITERAL < IF
    -1 TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ 3 LSHIFT LSHIFT INVERT AND
    DUP 1 TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ 3 LSHIFT 1 - LSHIFT AND IF -1 TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ 3 LSHIFT LSHIFT OR THEN
  THEN ;
: LIT+ ( n --- ) T-NORM O-LIT SWAP 0 0 OP+ ;
: ALIT+ ( t-addr --- ) T-NORM O-LIT SWAP 1 0 OP+ ;    \ 715: an address (['] ) - b 1: never factored, it moves
: BR+ ( target long short --- ) >R >R O-BR SWAP R> R> OP+ ;
: STR+ ( c-addr u --- )
  DUP SPOOL# @ + 8192 > ABORT" cross: a definition's strings too long"
  >R SPOOL SPOOL# @ + R@ CMOVE O-STR SPOOL SPOOL# @ + R@ 0 OP+ R> SPOOL# +! ;
: >FWD-BR ( long short --- j ) #OPS @ >R -1 ROT ROT BR+ R> ;
: >RESOLVE ( j --- ) #OPS @ DUP MARK SWAP OP# CELL+ ! ;

\ ---- the passes: the image is built three times over (PART 10). The
\ first finds the dead words - a word defined again under its name that
\ nothing calls, POSTPONEs or takes the address of (the translator's dead
\ shadowed words, --drop-dumptool) - and whether every call reaches below
\ 16 KB; the second leaves the dead words out and counts the call sites;
\ the third gives the most-called words one-byte calls (the translator's
\ --hotcalls), and it is the image. A word is known from pass to pass by
\ its ordinal: the shadows are made in the same order every time.
2048 CONSTANT #ORD-MAX
VARIABLE PASS 0 PASS !
CREATE DEAD #ORD-MAX ALLOT  DEAD #ORD-MAX 0 FILL    \ from the pass before: left out
CREATE REFD #ORD-MAX ALLOT                         \ called, POSTPONEd or its address taken
CREATE ORD-SH #ORD-MAX CELLS ALLOT                 \ ordinal -> shadow
CREATE FREE# #ORD-MAX CELLS ALLOT                  \ call sites not before an inline cell
CREATE ALL# #ORD-MAX CELLS ALLOT                   \ ...and all of them
CREATE HOTS 32 CELLS ALLOT  VARIABLE #HOTS 0 #HOTS !   \ from the pass before: one-byte calls' targets
VARIABLE DEAD-NOW 0 DEAD-NOW !     \ the word being made is dead: nothing of it in the image
VARIABLE COUNTING 0 COUNTING !     \ this pass counts call sites
VARIABLE #SHADOWS 0 #SHADOWS !     \ the shadows made so far: the next one's ordinal
\ A shadow's ordinal, its one-byte call, its name (PART 4's shadows).
: ORD ( shadow --- k ) 11 CELLS + @ ;
: HOT-OF ( shadow --- code | 0 ) 10 CELLS + @ ;
: SH-NAME ( shadow --- c-addr u ) 15 CELLS + COUNT ;
: PENDING? ( shadow --- f ) 13 CELLS + @ ;
: REF! ( shadow --- )
  DUP ORD DEAD + C@ IF ." cross: " SH-NAME TYPE CR -1 ABORT" cross: a dead word referenced" THEN
  ORD REFD + 1 SWAP C! ;
: HOT-CODE ( k --- code | 0 )
  #HOTS @ 0 ?DO DUP I CELLS HOTS + @ = IF DROP 224 I + UNLOOP EXIT THEN LOOP DROP 0 ;

\ ---- calls laid down before their target exists - a rebound name's, a
\ FORWARD's - are chained through their own bytes and made calls at the
\ end: two bytes where the image ends below 16 KB (NEAR, found by the
\ first pass), three otherwise, and none at all for a one-byte call (the
\ pass before found the target hot). A chain ends at CHAIN-END.
VARIABLE NEAR 0 NEAR !
: CHAIN-END ( --- n ) NEAR @ IF 16383 ELSE 16777215 THEN ;
: CHAIN-SIZE ( hot --- n )
\ A pending call's bytes: one if hot; two near; far three, or four under
\ the wide tag (it has no three-byte call).
  IF 1 ELSE NEAR @ IF 2 ELSE G-TAG2 G-T2WIDE AND IF 4 ELSE 3 THEN THEN THEN ;
: CHAIN,-T ( chain-a --- )
\ Bytes in the chain at chain-a: they hold the chain's old head, low
\ byte first.
  DUP @ THERE ROT !
  DUP 255 AND C,-T DUP 8 RSHIFT 255 AND C,-T
  0 CHAIN-SIZE 2 > IF DUP 16 RSHIFT 255 AND C,-T THEN DROP
  0 CHAIN-SIZE 3 > IF 0 C,-T THEN ;
: LINK@-T ( site --- link )
  DUP C@-T OVER 1+ C@-T 8 LSHIFT OR 0 CHAIN-SIZE 2 > IF SWAP 2 + C@-T 16 LSHIFT OR ELSE SWAP DROP THEN ;
: PATCH-CHAIN ( t-xt head --- )
\ Every link on a chain made a call to t-xt, laid down where it waited.
  BEGIN DUP CHAIN-END = 0= WHILE
    DUP LINK@-T >R                         ( t-xt site )   ( R: next )
    DP-T @ >R DP-T !  DUP 0 CHAIN-SIZE CALLN,-T  R> DP-T !
    R>
  REPEAT 2DROP ;
\ A call to a word: one byte where it is hot, chained while it waits for
\ its place (PART 6), else as near as its address allows.
: SITE-SIZE ( shadow --- n )
  DUP HOT-OF IF DROP 1 EXIT THEN DUP PENDING? IF DROP 0 CHAIN-SIZE EXIT THEN @ CALLSIZE-T ;
: SITE, ( shadow --- )
  DUP HOT-OF ?DUP IF C,-T DROP EXIT THEN
  DUP PENDING? IF 12 CELLS + CHAIN,-T EXIT THEN @ CALL-BYTES-T ;

\ ---- rebound names: the kernel's uses of words an overlay defines again
\ (the translator's --rebind) are calls to the last definition, resolved
\ at the end. A record: [name-a][name-u][chain][free sites][all sites]
\ [hot call, from the pass before].
CREATE RBS 32 6 * CELLS ALLOT   VARIABLE #RBS 0 #RBS !
: RB# ( k --- rec ) 6 * CELLS RBS + ;
: RB-INIT ( --- )
  0 #RBS !
  G-REBIND LIST-COUNT 0 ?DO
    I G-REBIND LIST-TOKEN #RBS @ RB# DUP >R CELL+ ! R@ ! 0 R> 5 CELLS + !
    1 #RBS +!
  LOOP ;
RB-INIT
: RB-RESET ( --- ) #RBS @ 0 ?DO CHAIN-END I RB# 2 CELLS + ! 0 I RB# 3 CELLS + ! 0 I RB# 4 CELLS + ! LOOP ;
: RB-OF ( c-addr u --- rec | 0 )
  #RBS @ 0 ?DO
    2DUP I RB# DUP @ SWAP CELL+ @ COMPARE 0= IF 2DROP I RB# UNLOOP EXIT THEN
  LOOP 2DROP 0 ;
: RB-SHADOW ( rec --- shadow )
  DUP @ SWAP CELL+ @ T-SHADOW 0= ABORT" cross: a rebound word never defined" ;
: RB-SITE-SIZE ( rec --- n ) 5 CELLS + @ CHAIN-SIZE ;
: RB-SITE, ( rec --- ) DUP 5 CELLS + @ ?DUP IF C,-T DROP ELSE 2 CELLS + CHAIN,-T THEN ;

\ ---- FORWARD: a word called before it is defined (COLD, THROW, the
\ runtimes the compiling words lay down); once the word exists, a call
\ at once. A record: [link][chain][free sites][all sites][hot call, from
\ the pass before][name].
VARIABLE FWD-LIST 0 FWD-LIST !
: FWD-NAME ( body --- c-addr u ) 5 CELLS + COUNT ;
: FWD-SHADOW ( body --- shadow | 0 ) FWD-NAME T-SHADOW 0= IF 0 THEN ;
: FWD-XT ( body --- t-xt -1 | 0 ) FWD-SHADOW ?DUP IF @ -1 ELSE 0 THEN ;
: FWD-REF ( body --- body ) DUP FWD-SHADOW ?DUP IF REF! THEN ;
: F+ ( fwd-body --- )
\ A call to a FORWARD; once the word exists, what its name compiles - a
\ format-10 word's opcode ((DO) where the design has it), a primitive's.
  DUP FWD-SHADOW ?DUP IF
    DUP CELL+ @ DUP K-PRIM = SWAP K-COLON = OR OVER 2 CELLS + @ AND IF
      DUP 2 CELLS + @ SWAP P+ DROP EXIT THEN
    REF!
  THEN O-F SWAP 0 0 OP+ ;
: FWD-SITE-SIZE ( body --- n )
  DUP FWD-SHADOW ?DUP IF SWAP DROP SITE-SIZE EXIT THEN 4 CELLS + @ CHAIN-SIZE ;
: FWD-SITE, ( body --- )
  DUP FWD-SHADOW ?DUP IF SWAP DROP SITE, EXIT THEN
  DUP 4 CELLS + @ ?DUP IF C,-T DROP EXIT THEN CELL+ CHAIN,-T ;
: FWD-CALL ( body --- )
\ Outside a definition (the boot vectors): no one-byte call there.
  DUP FWD-XT IF SWAP DROP CALL-BYTES-T EXIT THEN CELL+ CHAIN,-T ;
: FWD-RESET ( --- )
  FWD-LIST @ BEGIN ?DUP WHILE CHAIN-END OVER CELL+ ! 0 OVER 2 CELLS + ! 0 OVER 3 CELLS + ! @ REPEAT ;

: FORWARD ( "name" --- )
  >IN @ CREATE >IN !
  HERE FWD-LIST @ , FWD-LIST !  CHAIN-END , 0 , 0 , 0 ,
  BL WORD COUNT DUP C, HERE SWAP DUP ALLOT CMOVE ALIGN
  DOES> STATE-T @ IF F+ ELSE FWD-CALL THEN ;

: RESOLVE-FORWARDS ( --- )
  FWD-LIST @ BEGIN ?DUP WHILE
    DUP CELL+ @ CHAIN-END = 0= IF
      DUP FWD-XT 0= IF ." cross: unresolved " DUP FWD-NAME TYPE CR -1 ABORT" cross: a forward reference never defined" THEN
      OVER CELL+ @ PATCH-CHAIN
    THEN @
  REPEAT ;
: RESOLVE-REBINDS ( --- )
  #RBS @ 0 ?DO
    I RB# DUP 2 CELLS + @ CHAIN-END = 0= IF
      DUP RB-SHADOW @ SWAP 2 CELLS + @ PATCH-CHAIN
    ELSE DROP THEN
  LOOP ;

\ ---- the rewrites ------------------------------------------------------
: SPECIALISE ( --- )
\ var: a data word's call then @ or ! - VF or VS. imm: LIT n then + or =,
\ n in -128..127 - ADDI or EQI.
  #OPS @ 1 > 0= IF EXIT THEN
  #OPS @ 1- 0 ?DO
    I 1+ TGT? 0= I 1+ OP-K O-P = AND IF
      I OP-K O-DC = 4 SPEC? AND IF
        I 1+ OP-A DUP 2 SPECIAL = SWAP 3 SPECIAL = OR IF
          O-SLOT I 1+ OP-A 2 SPECIAL = IF 99 ELSE 100 THEN I OP-B I OP-C I OP! I 1+ KILL   \ c: its shadow (715)
        THEN
      THEN
      I OP-K O-LIT = 2 SPEC? AND IF
        I OP-A DUP -128 < 0= SWAP 128 < AND IF
          I 1+ OP-A DUP 0 SPECIAL = SWAP 1 SPECIAL = OR IF
            O-IMM I 1+ OP-A 0 SPECIAL = IF 120 ELSE 122 THEN I OP-A 0 I OP! I 1+ KILL
          THEN
        THEN
      THEN
    THEN
  LOOP ;

: EXIT-OP? ( i --- f ) DUP OP-K O-P = SWAP OP-A 1 = AND ;
: FOLD-PASS ( --- )
\ An operation and the EXIT after it, one opcode (fold_exit): a fold-set
\ primitive, ADDI, EQI, a literal below 64 KB if LIT is in the set.
  #OPS @ 1 > 0= IF EXIT THEN
  #OPS @ 1- 0 ?DO
    I 1+ EXIT-OP? I 1+ TGT? 0= AND IF
      I OP-K O-P = I OP-A 128 < AND IF I OP-A CHARS FOLDMAP + C@ ?DUP IF O-P SWAP 0 0 I OP! I 1+ KILL THEN THEN
      I OP-K O-IMM = IF I OP-A 1 AND 0= IF O-IMM I OP-A 1+ I OP-B 0 I OP! I 1+ KILL THEN THEN
      I OP-K O-LIT = IF I OP-A DUP 0< 0= SWAP 65536 < AND 2 FOLDMAP + C@ 0= 0= AND IF
        O-LITX I OP-A 0 0 I OP! I 1+ KILL THEN THEN
    THEN
  LOOP ;

\ The design's pairs as opcodes, as their words come to exist - a pair
\ may name a format-10 word, defined after the primitives.
CREATE PAIRS 64 3 * CELLS ALLOT  VARIABLE #PAIRS 0 #PAIRS !  VARIABLE PAIRS-OPEN -1 PAIRS-OPEN !
: OP-OF-SHADOW ( shadow --- op | -1 )
  DUP CELL+ @ K-PRIM = IF 2 CELLS + @ EXIT THEN 2 CELLS + @ ?DUP 0= IF -1 THEN ;
: NAME-OP ( c-addr u --- op | -1 ) T-SHADOW IF OP-OF-SHADOW ELSE -1 THEN ;
: PAIRS-INIT ( --- )
  0 #PAIRS ! 0 PAIRS-OPEN !
  G-SUPERS LIST-COUNT 3 / 0 ?DO
    I 3 * G-SUPERS LIST-TOKEN NAME-OP
    I 3 * 1+ G-SUPERS LIST-TOKEN NAME-OP
    2DUP 0< SWAP 0< OR IF 1 PAIRS-OPEN +! THEN
    I 3 * 2 + G-SUPERS LIST-TOKEN TOKEN>N
    #PAIRS @ 3 * CELLS PAIRS + DUP >R 2 CELLS + ! R@ CELL+ ! R> !
    1 #PAIRS +!
  LOOP ;
: PAIR? ( op1 op2 --- op | 0 )
  #PAIRS @ 0 ?DO
    OVER I 3 * CELLS PAIRS + @ = OVER I 3 * CELLS PAIRS + CELL+ @ = AND IF
      2DROP I 3 * CELLS PAIRS + 2 CELLS + @ UNLOOP EXIT THEN
  LOOP 2DROP 0 ;
: PAIR-PASS ( --- )
  PAIRS-OPEN @ IF PAIRS-INIT THEN
  #OPS @ 1 > 0= IF EXIT THEN
  #OPS @ 1- 0 ?DO
    I OP-K O-P = I 1+ OP-K O-P = AND I 1+ TGT? 0= AND IF
      I OP-A I 1+ OP-A PAIR? ?DUP IF O-P SWAP 0 0 I OP! I 1+ KILL THEN
    THEN
  LOOP ;

\ What the cross compiler does not do yet refuses the design (the genes'
\ G-NOT-YET: the translator's options it has no rule for).
: NOT-YET? ( --- )
  G-NOT-YET DUP IF S" cross: not yet: " TYPE TYPE CR -1 ABORT" cross: the design needs what this compiler does not do yet" THEN 2DROP ;
NOT-YET?

\ Iteration 714: the gene abortif (the translator's --guard-abort,
\ sod16.py's guard_aborts) - the genes' G-GUARD-ABORT, 0 for genes written
\ before it (designs/*/genes.4 of the ten shipped designs).
CREATE GA-NAME 13 C, 71 C, 45 C, 71 C, 85 C, 65 C, 82 C, 68 C, 45 C, 65 C, 66 C, 79 C, 82 C, 84 C,
: GA-GENE ( --- f ) GA-NAME FIND IF EXECUTE ELSE DROP 0 THEN ;
GA-GENE CONSTANT GUARD-ABORT?

: TEST-PASS ( --- )
\ A test, then a ?BRANCH nothing lands on: the fused branch, where the
\ design has it - the test's shadow carries the opcodes.
  #OPS @ 1 > 0= IF EXIT THEN
  #OPS @ 1- 0 ?DO
    I 1+ OP-K O-BR = I 1+ OP-B 4 = AND I 1+ TGT? 0= AND
    I OP-K O-P = I OP-K O-C = OR AND I OP-C 0= 0= AND IF
      I OP-C 6 CELLS + @ ?DUP IF
        O-BR I 1+ OP-A ROT I OP-C 7 CELLS + @ I OP! I 1+ KILL
      THEN
    THEN
  LOOP ;

\ Iteration 722: tools/sod16.py's eqibranch - EQI n then a ?BRANCH nothing
\ lands on, as =I?BRANCH (=I?BRANCH8 where it fits and the design has it):
\ the opcode, n's byte, the offset from itself (vm-lab.c's L_x_eqibr). One
\ operation here, O-EQBR, where the translator keeps two in place (EQIH,
\ EQIT) - the same bytes. After the tests, as there: the EQI is not one.
S" =I?BRANCH" OPS10-OF CONSTANT X-EQIBR
S" =I?BRANCH8" OPS10-OF X-EQIBR 0= 0= AND CONSTANT X-EQIBR8   \ the short needs the long, as shorten()'s
: EQI-PASS ( --- )
  X-EQIBR 0= IF EXIT THEN
  #OPS @ 1 > 0= IF EXIT THEN
  #OPS @ 1- 0 ?DO
    I OP-K O-IMM = I OP-A 122 = AND
    I 1+ OP-K O-BR = AND I 1+ OP-B 4 = AND I 1+ TGT? 0= AND IF
      O-EQBR I 1+ OP-A I OP-B X-EQIBR8 I OP! I 1+ KILL
    THEN
  LOOP ;

\ tools/sod16.py's keepbranch: SWAP or DUP before an ADDI, as SWAP+I and
\ DUP+I; DUP n < as DUP<I (n in -128..127); DUP before the fused 0=
\ ?BRANCH, as DUP?NBRANCH (722; DUP?NBRANCH8 where it fits) - where nothing
\ lands on what is taken in.
S" SWAP+I" OPS10-OF CONSTANT X-SADDI
S" DUP+I" OPS10-OF CONSTANT X-DADDI
S" DUP<I" OPS10-OF CONSTANT X-DLTI
S" 0=" TEST-OPS DROP CONSTANT X-NQBR            \ the fused 0= ?BRANCH's long opcode, or 0
S" DUP?NBRANCH" OPS10-OF X-NQBR 0= 0= AND CONSTANT X-DNBR
S" DUP?NBRANCH8" OPS10-OF X-DNBR 0= 0= AND CONSTANT X-DNBR8
: DNBR-AT? ( i --- f ) DUP OP-K O-BR = SWAP OP-B X-NQBR = AND X-DNBR 0= 0= AND ;
: ADDI-AT? ( i --- f ) DUP OP-K O-IMM = SWAP OP-A 120 = AND ;
: DLTI-AT? ( i --- f )
\ DUP at i - n < after it, nothing landing on them.
  DUP 2 + #OPS @ < 0= IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP 1+ OP-K O-LIT = 0= IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP 1+ OP-A DUP -128 < 0= SWAP 128 < AND 0= IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP 2 + TGT? IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP 2 + OP-K O-P = SWAP 2 + OP-A 6 SPECIAL = AND ;
: KEEP-PASS ( --- )
  X-SADDI X-DADDI OR X-DLTI OR X-DNBR OR 0= IF EXIT THEN
  #OPS @ 1 > 0= IF EXIT THEN
  #OPS @ 1- 0 ?DO
    I OP-K O-P = I 1+ TGT? 0= AND IF
      I OP-A 5 SPECIAL = I 1+ ADDI-AT? AND X-SADDI AND IF
        O-IMM X-SADDI I 1+ OP-B 0 I OP! I 1+ KILL
      ELSE I OP-A 4 SPECIAL = IF
        I 1+ DNBR-AT? IF
          O-BR I 1+ OP-A X-DNBR X-DNBR8 I OP! I 1+ KILL
        ELSE I 1+ ADDI-AT? X-DADDI AND IF
          O-IMM X-DADDI I 1+ OP-B 0 I OP! I 1+ KILL
        ELSE I DLTI-AT? X-DLTI AND IF
          O-IMM X-DLTI I 1+ OP-A 0 I OP! I 1+ KILL I 2 + KILL
        THEN THEN THEN
      THEN THEN
    THEN
  LOOP ;

\ ---- layout and encoding --------------------------------------------
: LIT-OP ( n --- op )
\ The narrowest literal that holds n: with small, 0, 1 and -1 one
\ operation (LIT0, LIT1, LITM1); then cv8.4's LIT, - LIT8, LIT16 (the LIT
\ primitive), LIT32 (sign-extended), LIT64.
  1 SPEC? IF DUP 0 = IF DROP 96 EXIT THEN DUP 1 = IF DROP 97 EXIT THEN DUP -1 = IF DROP 98 EXIT THEN THEN
  DUP 0< 0= OVER 256 < AND IF DROP 71 EXIT THEN
  DUP 0< 0= OVER 65536 < AND IF DROP 2 EXIT THEN
  TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ 4 = IF DROP 68 EXIT THEN
  2147483648 + 4294967296 U< IF 68 ELSE 124 THEN ;
: LIT-SIZE ( n --- size )
  LIT-OP DUP OPSIZE-T SWAP                        ( size op )
  DUP 71 = IF DROP 1+ EXIT THEN  DUP 2 = IF DROP 2 + EXIT THEN
  DUP 68 = IF DROP 4 + EXIT THEN  124 = IF 8 + THEN ;
: LIT,-T ( n --- )
  DUP LIT-OP DUP OP,-T
  DUP 71 = IF DROP C,-T EXIT THEN  DUP 2 = IF DROP W,-T EXIT THEN
  DUP 68 = IF DROP 32,-T EXIT THEN  124 = IF DUP 32,-T 32 RSHIFT 32,-T EXIT THEN
  DROP ;
: LITX,-T ( n --- ) DUP 256 < IF 72 OP,-T C,-T ELSE 2 FOLDMAP + C@ OP,-T W,-T THEN ;

: PADDED ( addr n --- pad )
\ The NOOPs before a call of n bytes that leave the cell after it aligned.
  + TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ 1- AND DUP IF TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ SWAP - THEN ;
: ADDR ( i --- addr ) CELLS ADDRS + @ ;

: S-0 ( addr i --- n ) 2DROP 0 ;
: S-1 ( addr i --- n ) 2DROP 1 ;
: S-2 ( addr i --- n ) 2DROP 2 ;
: S-3 ( addr i --- n ) 2DROP 3 ;
: S-C ( addr i --- n ) SWAP DROP OP-C SITE-SIZE ;
: S-F ( addr i --- n ) SWAP DROP OP-A FWD-SITE-SIZE ;
: S-RB ( addr i --- n ) SWAP DROP OP-A RB-SITE-SIZE ;
: S-LIT ( addr i --- n ) SWAP DROP OP-A LIT-SIZE ;
: S-LITX ( addr i --- n ) SWAP DROP OP-A 256 < IF 72 OPSIZE-T 1+ ELSE 2 FOLDMAP + C@ OPSIZE-T 2 + THEN ;
: SHORT? ( i --- f ) DUP OP-C 0= 0= SWAP LONG + C@ 0= AND ;
: S-BR ( addr i --- n ) SWAP DROP DUP SHORT? IF OP-C OPSIZE-T 1+ ELSE OP-B OPSIZE-T 2 + THEN ;
: S-SLOT ( addr i --- n ) SWAP DROP DUP OP-A OPSIZE-T SWAP OP-B SLOTSIZE-T + ;
: S-IMM ( addr i --- n ) SWAP DROP OP-A OPSIZE-T 1+ ;
: OPDC-CALL ( i --- n )
\ The call before an inline cell: under the tag always the four-byte
\ form (layout.py's pad_before), else as near as it reaches.
  G-TAG2 IF DROP 4 ELSE OP-A FWD-SITE-SIZE THEN ;
: S-OPDC ( addr i --- n ) OPDC-CALL DUP >R PADDED R> + TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ + ;
: S-STR ( addr i --- n ) OP-B 1+ SWAP DROP ;    \ 681: the count and the characters, unpadded (cv8.4's (S")8)

: E-DEAD ( i --- ) DROP ;
: E-P ( i --- ) OP-A OP,-T ;
: S-P ( addr i --- n ) SWAP DROP OP-A OPSIZE-T ;
: E-C ( i --- ) OP-C SITE, ;
: E-F ( i --- ) OP-A FWD-SITE, ;
: E-RB ( i --- ) OP-A RB-SITE, ;
: E-LIT ( i --- ) OP-A LIT,-T ;
: E-LITX ( i --- ) OP-A LITX,-T ;
: BR-OFFSET ( i op --- offset )
\ A branch's offset, from its operand - past the opcode's bytes (and
\ =I?BRANCH's immediate byte: 722).
  OPSIZE-T OVER ADDR + OVER OP-K O-EQBR = IF 1+ THEN SWAP OP-A ADDR SWAP - ;
: E-BR ( i --- )
  >R R@ SHORT? IF
    R@ R@ OP-C BR-OFFSET R> OP-C OP,-T 255 AND C,-T
  ELSE
    R@ R@ OP-B BR-OFFSET R> OP-B OP,-T DUP -32768 < OVER 32767 > OR ABORT" cross: branch too long" W,-T
  THEN ;
: S-EQBR ( addr i --- n ) SWAP DROP SHORT? IF X-EQIBR8 OPSIZE-T 2 + ELSE X-EQIBR OPSIZE-T 3 + THEN ;
: E-EQBR ( i --- )
\ 722: =I?BRANCH, n's byte, the offset from itself.
  >R R@ SHORT? IF
    R@ X-EQIBR8 BR-OFFSET X-EQIBR8 OP,-T R> OP-B 255 AND C,-T 255 AND C,-T
  ELSE
    R@ X-EQIBR BR-OFFSET X-EQIBR OP,-T R> OP-B 255 AND C,-T
    DUP -32768 < OVER 32767 > OR ABORT" cross: branch too long" W,-T
  THEN ;
: E-SLOT ( i --- ) DUP OP-A OP,-T OP-B SLOT,-T ;
: E-IMM ( i --- ) DUP OP-A OP,-T OP-B 255 AND C,-T ;
: E-OPDC ( i --- )
\ NOOPs, the call, and the aligned cell after it: a loop's back offset,
\ or (POSTPONE)'s xt, from the cell itself.
  >R R@ OPDC-CALL THERE SWAP PADDED 0 ?DO 0 C,-T LOOP
  G-TAG2 IF R@ OP-A FWD-XT 0= ABORT" cross: a call before an inline cell to a word not yet defined" 4 CALLN,-T
  ELSE R@ OP-A FWD-SITE, THEN
  R@ OP-K O-LOOPC = IF R@ OP-B ADDR THERE - ,-T R> DROP EXIT THEN
  R@ OP-C DUP PENDING? IF 14 CELLS + DUP @ SWAP THERE SWAP ! ,-T ELSE @ THERE - ,-T THEN R> DROP ;
: E-STR ( i --- )
  DUP OP-B DUP C,-T SWAP OP-A THERE CHARS IMAGE + ROT DUP ALLOT-T CMOVE ;    \ 681: no ALIGN-T after it

\ A buffer word's LIT32 (the translator's LITOFF), patched at the end.
14 CONSTANT O-LIT32
VARIABLE LIT32-AT
: S-5 ( addr i --- n ) 2DROP 68 OPSIZE-T 4 + ;
: E-LIT32 ( i --- ) DROP 68 OP,-T THERE LIT32-AT ! 0 32,-T ;

CREATE SIZERS 17 CELLS ALLOT
CREATE ENCODERS 17 CELLS ALLOT
: KIND! ( sizer encoder kind --- ) CELLS DUP >R ENCODERS + ! R> SIZERS + ! ;
' S-0 ' E-DEAD O-DEAD KIND!
' S-P ' E-P O-P KIND!
' S-C ' E-C O-C KIND!
' S-F ' E-F O-F KIND!
' S-LIT ' E-LIT O-LIT KIND!
' S-BR ' E-BR O-BR KIND!
' S-C ' E-C O-DC KIND!
' S-OPDC ' E-OPDC O-LOOPC KIND!
' S-OPDC ' E-OPDC O-PPC KIND!
' S-STR ' E-STR O-STR KIND!
' S-SLOT ' E-SLOT O-SLOT KIND!
' S-IMM ' E-IMM O-IMM KIND!
' S-LITX ' E-LITX O-LITX KIND!
' S-RB ' E-RB O-RB KIND!
' S-5 ' E-LIT32 O-LIT32 KIND!
' S-EQBR ' E-EQBR O-EQBR KIND!
\ 715: the gene factor's genes (export-genes.py; 0 in genes written before
\ it) and its call: O-FB, a call to a factored body - chained, the bodies
\ laid after the last word (the factor section, below END-DEF's).
CREATE GBUF 34 ALLOT
: GENE ( c-addr u --- xt | 0 ) GBUF PLACE GBUF FIND 0= IF DROP 0 THEN ;
: GENE-N ( c-addr u --- x ) GENE DUP IF EXECUTE THEN ;
S" G-FACTOR" GENE-N G-TAG2 AND CONSTANT FACTOR?
S" G-FACTOR-ANY" GENE-N CONSTANT FAC-ANY
S" G-FACTOR-COLD" GENE CONSTANT FAC-COLD-XT
S" G-FACTOR-NOT" GENE CONSTANT FAC-NOT-XT
: FAC-LIST ( xt|0 --- c-addr u ) ?DUP IF EXECUTE ELSE 0 0 THEN ;
: FAC-CHECK ( --- ) FACTOR? G-HOTCALLS AND ABORT" cross: factor with one-byte calls not done (the tag has none)" ;
FAC-CHECK
256 CONSTANT #FB-MAX
CREATE FB-CHAIN #FB-MAX CELLS FACTOR? AND ALLOT     \ a body's chain of calls
CREATE FB-SNAP #FB-MAX FACTOR? AND ALLOT            \ its operations kept, this pass
15 CONSTANT O-FB
: S-FB ( addr i --- n ) 2DROP 0 CHAIN-SIZE ;
: E-FB ( i --- ) OP-A CELLS FB-CHAIN + CHAIN,-T ;
' S-FB ' E-FB O-FB KIND!
: OP-SIZE ( addr i --- n ) DUP OP-K CELLS SIZERS + @ EXECUTE ;
: OP-ENCODE ( i --- ) DUP OP-K CELLS ENCODERS + @ EXECUTE ;

: LAYOUT ( base --- )
  #OPS @ 0 ?DO DUP I CELLS ADDRS + ! DUP I OP-SIZE + LOOP #OPS @ CELLS ADDRS + ! ;
VARIABLE CHANGED
: RELAX ( base --- )
\ Short forms wherever their offsets fit: lay out, send the misfits long,
\ again - a long branch never comes back, so it ends.
  LONG #OPS-MAX 0 FILL
  BEGIN
    DUP LAYOUT 0 CHANGED !
    #OPS @ 0 ?DO
      I BR? IF
        I OP-A 0< ABORT" cross: a branch never resolved"
        I SHORT? IF
          I I OP-C BR-OFFSET DUP -128 < SWAP 127 > OR IF 1 I LONG + C! -1 CHANGED ! THEN
        THEN
      THEN
    LOOP
  CHANGED @ 0= UNTIL DROP ;
: ENCODE ( --- )
  #OPS @ 0 ?DO
    I ADDR THERE = 0= ABORT" cross: the layout drifted"
    I OP-ENCODE
  LOOP
  #OPS @ ADDR THERE = 0= ABORT" cross: the layout drifted at the end" ;
\ The call sites of a definition's final operations: a call before an
\ inline cell counts only among all (its cell stays aligned, so what a
\ one-byte call saves there depends on where it lands - layout.py).
: SITE+ ( shadow free? --- ) SWAP ORD CELLS >R IF 1 R@ FREE# + +! THEN 1 R> ALL# + +! ;
: FSITE+ ( body free? --- )
  OVER FWD-SHADOW ?DUP IF ROT DROP SWAP SITE+ EXIT THEN
  IF 1 OVER 2 CELLS + +! THEN 1 SWAP 3 CELLS + +! ;
: COUNT-SITES ( --- )
  #OPS @ 0 ?DO
    I OP-K
    DUP O-C = OVER O-DC = OR IF I OP-C -1 SITE+ THEN
    DUP O-F = IF I OP-A -1 FSITE+ THEN
    DUP O-RB = IF 1 I OP-A 3 CELLS + +! 1 I OP-A 4 CELLS + +! THEN
    DUP O-LOOPC = OVER O-PPC = OR IF I OP-A 0 FSITE+ THEN
    DROP
  LOOP ;
\ ---- hot calls inlined (the translator's --hot-inline: tools/sod16.py's
\ hot_inline, Iteration 92). G-HOT-INLINE names the sites - caller, callee
\ and k, the k-th call to callee in caller's body, by their final names
\ (the last X8's is its X's) - and at each the callee's body as compiled,
\ before any rewrite, takes the call's place, for the rewrites to see it
\ there. A callee's body is kept as it ends, its words by their ordinals;
\ a callee made after its caller is inlined from the pass before's (in
\ the first pass not at all: the call stays), and a word in it the pass
\ has not made yet is called through a chain on its shadow of the pass
\ before, made calls when the pass ends. The callee stays referenced.
512 CONSTANT #RAW-MAX
CREATE RAW-OPS #RAW-MAX 4 * CELLS ALLOT  VARIABLE RAW# 0 RAW# !
CREATE RAW-AT #ORD-MAX CELLS ALLOT  RAW-AT #ORD-MAX CELLS 0 FILL  \ ordinal -> its kept body's first op + 1, or 0
CREATE RAW-N #ORD-MAX CELLS ALLOT                                 \ ...and its length
VARIABLE HS-ON  0 HS-ON !          \ this body is a caller a site names
VARIABLE HS-STORE  0 HS-STORE !    \ ...a callee's: its final shadow
VARIABLE HS-FINAL  0 HS-FINAL !    \ ...the code its name runs (not an X8 before the last)
CREATE HS-FNAME 34 ALLOT           \ ...its final name
CREATE HS-CNT 128 CELLS ALLOT  VARIABLE #HS-CNT 0 #HS-CNT !   \ [shadow][calls so far]
CREATE FWDP 64 CELLS ALLOT  VARIABLE #FWDP 0 #FWDP !   \ shadows of the pass before holding chains
VARIABLE HS-R
: HS-TRIPLES ( --- n ) G-HOT-INLINE LIST-COUNT 3 / ;
: HS-ROLE? ( c-addr u role --- f )
\ Does a site name this caller (role 0) or callee (role 1)?
  HS-R ! HS-TRIPLES 0 ?DO
    2DUP I 3 * HS-R @ + G-HOT-INLINE LIST-TOKEN COMPARE 0= IF 2DROP UNLOOP -1 EXIT THEN
  LOOP 2DROP 0 ;
: HS-SITE? ( c-addr u k --- f )
\ Is the k-th call to this callee in this body a site?
  HS-R ! HS-TRIPLES 0 ?DO
    HS-FNAME COUNT I 3 * G-HOT-INLINE LIST-TOKEN COMPARE 0= IF
      2DUP I 3 * 1+ G-HOT-INLINE LIST-TOKEN COMPARE 0= IF
        I 3 * 2 + G-HOT-INLINE LIST-TOKEN TOKEN>N HS-R @ = IF 2DROP UNLOOP -1 EXIT THEN
      THEN
    THEN
  LOOP 2DROP 0 ;
: HS-COUNT ( shadow --- k )
  #HS-CNT @ 0 ?DO
    DUP I 2* CELLS HS-CNT + @ = IF DROP I 2* 1+ CELLS HS-CNT + DUP @ 1+ DUP ROT ! UNLOOP EXIT THEN
  LOOP
  #HS-CNT @ 64 < 0= ABORT" cross: too many callees in a hot-inline caller"
  #HS-CNT @ 2* CELLS HS-CNT + !  1 #HS-CNT @ 2* 1+ CELLS HS-CNT + !  1 #HS-CNT +! 1 ;
CREATE HS-LOG 16 5 * CELLS ALLOT  VARIABLE #HS-LOG 0 #HS-LOG !   \ the splices so far: [first op][ops][kind][a][c]
: HS-BEGIN ( final-shadow --- )
\ At a body's start (the colon twin): the roles the sites give it.
  0 #HS-CNT ! 0 #HS-LOG ! 0 HS-ON ! 0 HS-STORE !
  HS-FINAL @ 0= IF DROP EXIT THEN
  HS-FNAME COUNT 0 HS-ROLE? HS-ON !
  HS-FNAME COUNT 1 HS-ROLE? IF HS-STORE ! ELSE DROP THEN ;
: HS-LOG-OPEN ( shadow --- )
\ A splice starts here, in place of the operation REF-T makes for the
\ call: an op-body word's opcode, else the call.
  #HS-LOG @ 16 < 0= ABORT" cross: too many hot-inline sites in a word"
  #HS-LOG @ 5 * CELLS HS-LOG + >R
  #OPS @ R@ !  DUP R@ 4 CELLS + !
  DUP 2 CELLS + @ ?DUP IF O-P R@ 2 CELLS + ! R@ 3 CELLS + ! DROP ELSE O-C R@ 2 CELLS + ! @ R@ 3 CELLS + ! THEN
  R> DROP ;
: HS-LOG-CLOSE ( --- ) #OPS @ #HS-LOG @ 5 * CELLS HS-LOG + DUP @ ROT SWAP - SWAP CELL+ ! 1 #HS-LOG +! ;
: HS-LOGGED ( i --- entry | 0 )
  #HS-LOG @ 0 ?DO I 5 * CELLS HS-LOG + DUP @ 2 PICK = IF SWAP DROP UNLOOP EXIT THEN DROP LOOP DROP 0 ;
: RAW-OK? ( i --- f )
\ A straight-line operation (sod16.py's inline_body): a plain one, not
\ EXIT; a call; a literal.
  DUP OP-K O-P = IF OP-A 1 = 0= EXIT THEN
  OP-K DUP O-C = OVER O-LIT = OR OVER O-DC = OR SWAP O-RB = OR ;
: RAW-ORD ( shadow|0 --- ord|-1 ) ?DUP IF ORD ELSE -1 THEN ;
CREATE RAW-TMP 256 4 * CELLS ALLOT  VARIABLE #RAW-TMP
: TMP+ ( k a b c --- )
  #RAW-TMP @ 256 < 0= ABORT" cross: a hot-inline callee too long"
  #RAW-TMP @ 4 * CELLS RAW-TMP + >R RAW-ORD R@ 3 CELLS + ! R@ 2 CELLS + ! R@ CELL+ ! R> ! 1 #RAW-TMP +! ;
: RAW-BUILD ( --- )
\ The body as compiled, each splice in it its call again (the translator
\ inlines a callee's body as read, before its own sites are), its words
\ by ordinal, the EXIT that ends it dropped.
  0 #RAW-TMP ! 0
  BEGIN DUP #OPS @ 1- < WHILE
    DUP HS-LOGGED ?DUP IF
      DUP 2 CELLS + @ OVER 3 CELLS + @ 0 3 PICK 4 CELLS + @ TMP+  CELL+ @ +
    ELSE
      DUP RAW-OK? 0= ABORT" cross: a hot-inline callee not straight-line"
      DUP OP-K OVER OP-A 2 PICK OP-B 3 PICK OP-C TMP+ 1+
    THEN
  REPEAT DROP ;
: RAW-KEEP ( final-shadow --- )
  #OPS @ 1- DUP OP-K O-P = SWAP OP-A 1 = AND 0= ABORT" cross: a hot-inline callee not ending in EXIT"
  RAW-BUILD
  ORD CELLS DUP RAW-AT + @ ?DUP IF                   ( off at+1 )
    1- OVER RAW-N + @ #RAW-TMP @ <> ABORT" cross: a hot-inline callee changed between passes"
  ELSE
    RAW# @ #RAW-TMP @ + #RAW-MAX > ABORT" cross: too many hot-inline callees"
    RAW# @ DUP 1+ 2 PICK RAW-AT + !  #RAW-TMP @ 2 PICK RAW-N + !  #RAW-TMP @ RAW# +!
  THEN SWAP DROP                                      ( first )
  4 * CELLS RAW-OPS +  RAW-TMP SWAP #RAW-TMP @ 4 * CELLS CMOVE ;
: HS-SH ( ord --- shadow ) CELLS ORD-SH + @ ;
: HS-OK? ( first n --- f )
\ Every word the kept body names made in this pass - or, not yet, an
\ operation's own name, or a call (no one-byte calls: a chain is two).
  0 ?DO
    DUP I + 4 * CELLS RAW-OPS +
    DUP 3 CELLS + @ #SHADOWS @ < 0= IF
      DUP @ O-C = G-HOTCALLS 0= AND OVER @ O-P = OR 0= IF 2DROP UNLOOP 0 EXIT THEN
    THEN DROP
  LOOP DROP -1 ;
: HS-PEND ( shadow --- )
\ A shadow of the pass before, for a word not made yet: calls to it chained.
  DUP PENDING? IF DROP EXIT THEN
  #FWDP @ 64 < 0= ABORT" cross: too many words called before they are made"
  DUP #FWDP @ CELLS FWDP + ! 1 #FWDP +!
  -2 OVER 13 CELLS + !  CHAIN-END SWAP 12 CELLS + ! ;
: HS-SPLICE ( first n --- )
  0 ?DO
    DUP I + 4 * CELLS RAW-OPS + >R                    \ (no I after >R)
    R@ 3 CELLS + @ DUP 0< IF DROP 0 ELSE HS-SH THEN   ( first shadow|0 )
    R@ @ O-C = IF
      DUP ORD #SHADOWS @ < 0= IF DUP HS-PEND THEN DUP REF! O-C OVER @ 0 3 PICK OP+
    ELSE R@ @ O-DC = IF O-DC OVER @ 2 PICK @ >BODY-T 3 PICK OP+
    ELSE R@ @ R@ CELL+ @ R@ 2 CELLS + @ 3 PICK OP+ THEN THEN
    DROP R> DROP
  LOOP DROP ;
: HS-TRY ( shadow --- shadow 0 | -1 )
\ A reference in a caller a site names (REF-T): counted, and at the site
\ the callee's kept body instead.
  HS-ON @ 0= IF 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP HS-COUNT >R DUP SH-NAME R> HS-SITE? 0= IF 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP ORD CELLS DUP RAW-AT + @ ?DUP 0= IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN    ( shadow off at+1 )
  1- SWAP RAW-N + @ 2DUP HS-OK? 0= IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN       ( shadow first n )
  ROT DUP REF! HS-LOG-OPEN HS-SPLICE HS-LOG-CLOSE -1 ;
: FWDP-PATCH ( --- )
\ At the pass's end: the chains on shadows of the pass before made calls
\ to the words made since.
  #FWDP @ 0 ?DO
    I CELLS FWDP + @ DUP ORD HS-SH                    ( old new )
    DUP PENDING? ABORT" cross: a word called before it is made never placed"
    @ OVER 12 CELLS + @ PATCH-CHAIN
    0 OVER 13 CELLS + !  CHAIN-END SWAP 12 CELLS + !
  LOOP 0 #FWDP ! ;

\ ---- the JIT's header on the image's own words (the translator's
\ --jitimg 1, Iteration 341): the outer interpreter's words begin as a
\ word compiled at run time does (cv8t-jit.4): [the JIT's code][the
\ body's length, top bit set] - translated at their first call. Only the
\ code their names run, with a header, and plain: no string, no cell
\ after a call (layout.py's _jitimg_pick).
: JH-NAMES ( --- c-addr u ) S" INTERPRET PARSE-WORD REFILL WORD ?STACK C, HERE CMOVE> PARSE (PARSE) SOURCE COMPILE, LITERAL NUMBER? (NUMBER?) >NUMBER FIND COUNT " ;
: JH-NAMED? ( --- f )
  G-JITIMG 1 > ABORT" cross: --jitimg 2 (every code word) not done"
  G-JITIMG HS-FINAL @ AND IF HS-FNAME COUNT JH-NAMES LIST-INDEX 0< 0= ELSE 0 THEN ;
: JH-PLAIN? ( --- f )
  TLINK @ 0= IF 0 EXIT THEN
  #OPS @ 0 ?DO I OP-K DUP O-STR = OVER O-LOOPC = OR SWAP O-PPC = OR IF UNLOOP 0 EXIT THEN LOOP -1 ;
: JIT-HEADER, ( len --- )
\ 723, the gene jitdead (layout.py --jit-dead, Iteration 710): the JIT's code alone - the native offset goes in the
\ translated body's first four bytes (engine/jit.c), so the body is made four bytes long (JD-PAD,).
  X-JITDEAD IF DROP 65533 OP,-T EXIT THEN 65533 OP,-T 1 31 LSHIFT OR 32,-T ;
CREATE JD-AT 64 CELLS ALLOT  CREATE JD-PAD 64 ALLOT  VARIABLE #JD  0 #JD !   \ jitdead: the headed bodies, their pads
: JD-PAD, ( xt len --- )
\ jitdead: NOOPs after the EXIT to four bytes of body, never run (layout.py's jh_pad); the pad kept for jit_wends.
  X-JITDEAD 0= IF 2DROP EXIT THEN
  4 SWAP - 0 MAX  #JD @ 64 < 0= ABORT" cross: more than 64 JIT-headed words"
  DUP #JD @ JD-PAD + C!  SWAP #JD @ CELLS JD-AT + !  1 #JD +!
  0 ?DO 0 C,-T LOOP ;
: JD-INDEX ( xt --- i | -1 ) #JD @ 0 ?DO DUP I CELLS JD-AT + @ = IF DROP I UNLOOP EXIT THEN LOOP DROP -1 ;
: JH-OPB ( len --- f ) JH-NAMED? TLINK @ 0= 0= AND IF JIT-HEADER, -1 ELSE DROP 0 THEN ;

\ ---- the gene factor (the translator's --factor: tools/layout.py,
\ Iteration 267; here 715). Repeated straight-line code in cold words
\ moved into headerless bodies [run][EXIT] after the last word, each use
\ a call. Pass 2 keeps the operations of every word it may factor - by
\ its final name in G-FACTOR-COLD (the reference profile's words below
\ --factor-share), or any with G-FACTOR-ANY, never G-FACTOR-NOT's - and
\ whether each word may be called from anywhere (sod16.py's ra_safe).
\ Between passes 2 and 3 the runs are found and chosen as layout.py does:
\ two to 16 operations of a stretch nothing lands on but its first, none
\ depending on where it sits (a branch, an inline cell, a string, an
\ address, an EXIT) or on the return stack below it (I, J, EXECUTE, the
\ loop words; a call to a word that reads its caller's return address;
\ >R and R> unbalanced), recurring, taken greedily by net bytes
\ k(len-2)-(len+1), a use never overlapping another. Pass 3 makes each
\ use a call (O-FB), checking it is what pass 2 kept, and lays the bodies
\ - the first use's operations as pass 3 has them - after the last word.
\ An operation is compared by what both passes see: a call by its word's
\ ordinal, a FORWARD's or rebound name's as the word it reached.
VARIABLE LAST-SHADOW 0 LAST-SHADOW !    \ the shadow made last (PART 4; here for the factor's use, 715)
VARIABLE FAC-ON  FACTOR? FAC-ON !
12288 CONSTANT #FE-MAX
10 CONSTANT FE-CELLS
\ An operation kept: [id-k][id-a][id-b][bytes][ordinal][index][landed][key-k][key-a][safe].
CREATE FE #FE-MAX FE-CELLS * CELLS FACTOR? AND ALLOT  VARIABLE #FE 0 #FE !
: FE# ( e --- a-addr ) FE-CELLS * CELLS FE + ;
: FE@ ( e n --- x ) CELLS SWAP FE# + @ ;
: FE! ( x e n --- ) CELLS SWAP FE# + ! ;
VARIABLE #FKEPT 0 #FKEPT !

: OP-ID ( i --- k a b )
\ An operation as two passes both see it: a call or a slot by its word's
\ ordinal (its address moves).
  DUP OP-K DUP O-C = OVER O-DC = OR IF SWAP OP-C ORD 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP O-SLOT = IF SWAP DUP OP-A SWAP OP-C ORD EXIT THEN
  SWAP DUP OP-A SWAP OP-B ;

\ The return stack below a body's entry (sod16.py's rs_walk), by opcode.
: RS-NAMES ( --- c-addr u ) S" >R 2>R R> RDROP 2R> R@ 2R@ RP@ RP! " ;
CREATE RS-NEED 0 , 0 , 1 , 1 , 2 , 1 , 2 , 99 , 99 ,
CREATE RS-DELTA 1 , 2 , -1 , -1 , -2 , 0 , 0 , 0 , 0 ,
CREATE RS-OPS 9 CELLS ALLOT
: RS-FILL ( --- ) 9 0 ?DO I RS-NAMES LIST-TOKEN NAME-OP I CELLS RS-OPS + ! LOOP ;
VARIABLE RS-D
: RS-STEP ( op --- f )
\ False where it reads below the entry, leaves by an EXIT off it, or
\ moves the stack pointer.
  DUP 1 = IF DROP RS-D @ 0= EXIT THEN
  9 0 ?DO
    DUP I CELLS RS-OPS + @ = IF
      DROP I CELLS RS-NEED + @ DUP 99 = IF DROP UNLOOP 0 EXIT THEN
      RS-D @ > IF UNLOOP 0 EXIT THEN
      I CELLS RS-DELTA + @ RS-D +! UNLOOP -1 EXIT
    THEN
  LOOP DROP -1 ;
: PAIR-OF ( op --- op1 op2 -1 | 0 )
  #PAIRS @ 0 ?DO
    DUP I 3 * CELLS PAIRS + 2 CELLS + @ = IF DROP I 3 * CELLS PAIRS + DUP @ SWAP CELL+ @ -1 UNLOOP EXIT THEN
  LOOP DROP 0 ;
: RS-OP ( op --- f ) DUP PAIR-OF IF ROT DROP SWAP RS-STEP IF RS-STEP ELSE DROP 0 THEN ELSE RS-STEP THEN ;
CREATE RSOK #ORD-MAX FACTOR? AND ALLOT             \ ordinal -> 1: it may be called from anywhere
: RS-KEEP ( --- )
\ Pass 2, before the rewrites (layout.py's raw_read): the definition's
\ own walk, not strict - for its word, and the X its last X8 replaces.
  RS-FILL 0 RS-D ! -1
  #OPS @ 0 ?DO I OP-K O-P = IF I OP-A RS-OP 0= IF DROP 0 LEAVE THEN THEN LOOP
  IF 1 ELSE 0 THEN DUP LAST-SHADOW @ ORD RSOK + C!
  HS-FINAL @ IF LAST-SHADOW @ 9 CELLS + @ ?DUP IF ORD RSOK + C! EXIT THEN THEN DROP ;   \ 9 CELLS +: >REDIR

CREATE LTG #OPS-MAX 1+ ALLOT
: LANDED ( --- )
\ What something lands on: the marks, a branch's target, a loop's start.
  TGTS LTG #OPS-MAX 1+ CMOVE
  #OPS @ 0 ?DO
    I BR? IF I OP-A DUP 0< 0= IF LTG + 1 SWAP C! ELSE DROP THEN THEN
    I OP-K O-LOOPC = IF 1 I OP-B LTG + C! THEN
  LOOP ;
: FAC-WORD? ( --- f )
  HS-FNAME COUNT FAC-NOT-XT FAC-LIST LIST-INDEX 0< 0= IF 0 EXIT THEN
  FAC-ANY IF -1 EXIT THEN
  HS-FNAME COUNT FAC-COLD-XT FAC-LIST LIST-INDEX 0< 0= ;
: FAC-KEEP ( --- )
\ Pass 2, after the rewrites: the word's operations.
  HS-FINAL @ 0= IF EXIT THEN
  FAC-WORD? 0= IF 1 #FKEPT +! EXIT THEN
  #FE @ #OPS @ + #FE-MAX > ABORT" cross: too many operations to factor"
  LANDED
  #OPS @ 0 ?DO
    I OP-ID #FE @ 2 FE! #FE @ 1 FE! #FE @ 0 FE!
    0 I OP-SIZE #FE @ 3 FE!  LAST-SHADOW @ ORD #FE @ 4 FE!  I #FE @ 5 FE!  I LTG + C@ #FE @ 6 FE!
    1 #FE +!
  LOOP ;

\ The search, between passes 2 and 3.
: RA-NAMES ( --- c-addr u ) S" EXECUTE I J UNLOOP (DO) (?DO) (LOOP) (+LOOP) (LEAVE) " ;
CREATE NOP-OPS 1024 FACTOR? AND ALLOT               \ opcode -> 1: never in a run
: NOP! ( op --- ) DUP 0< 0= OVER 1024 < AND IF NOP-OPS + 1 SWAP C! ELSE DROP THEN ;
: NOP? ( op --- f ) DUP 0< OVER 1023 > OR IF DROP -1 ELSE NOP-OPS + C@ 0= 0= THEN ;
: NOP-FILL ( --- )
\ EXIT, the words that read the return stack, every form with an EXIT
\ in it (the folds), a pair holding one.
  NOP-OPS 1024 0 FILL  1 NOP!
  RA-NAMES LIST-COUNT 0 ?DO I RA-NAMES LIST-TOKEN NAME-OP NOP! LOOP
  128 0 ?DO I FOLDMAP + C@ ?DUP IF NOP! THEN LOOP
  #PAIRS @ 0 ?DO
    I 3 * CELLS PAIRS + DUP @ NOP? SWAP CELL+ @ NOP? OR IF I 3 * CELLS PAIRS + 2 CELLS + @ NOP! THEN
  LOOP ;
: CALLEE-SAFE? ( shadow --- f )
  DUP CELL+ @ DUP K-DATA = SWAP K-CONST = OR IF DROP -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP CELL+ @ K-COLON = 0= IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP SH-NAME RA-NAMES LIST-INDEX 0< 0= IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  ORD RSOK + C@ 0= 0= ;
: FE-SAFE ( e --- f )
  DUP 0 FE@
  DUP O-P = IF DROP 1 FE@ NOP? 0= EXIT THEN
  DUP O-LIT = IF DROP 2 FE@ 0= EXIT THEN
  DUP O-SLOT = OVER O-DC = OR IF 2DROP -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP O-IMM = IF DROP 1 FE@ DUP 121 <> SWAP 123 <> AND EXIT THEN
  DUP O-C = IF DROP 1 FE@ HS-SH CALLEE-SAFE? EXIT THEN
  DUP O-F = IF DROP 1 FE@ FWD-SHADOW ?DUP IF CALLEE-SAFE? ELSE 0 THEN EXIT THEN
  DUP O-RB = IF DROP 1 FE@ RB-SHADOW CALLEE-SAFE? EXIT THEN
  2DROP 0 ;
: FE-KEY ( e --- )
  >R R@ 0 FE@ R@ 1 FE@
  OVER O-F = IF 2DROP O-C R@ 1 FE@ FWD-SHADOW ?DUP IF ORD ELSE -1 THEN THEN
  OVER O-RB = IF 2DROP O-C R@ 1 FE@ RB-SHADOW ORD THEN
  R@ 8 FE! R> 7 FE! ;
CREATE FE-END #FE-MAX CELLS FACTOR? AND ALLOT       \ an operation's stretch's end, or 0
: FE-SEGS ( --- )
\ In each word the stretches of safe operations nothing lands on but the
\ first (layout.py's _segs).
  #FE @ 0 ?DO 0 I CELLS FE-END + ! LOOP
  0 BEGIN DUP #FE @ < WHILE                        ( j )
    DUP 9 FE@ 0= IF 1+ ELSE
      DUP 1+ BEGIN                                 ( i j )
        DUP #FE @ < IF DUP 9 FE@ OVER 6 FE@ 0= AND OVER 4 FE@ 3 PICK 4 FE@ = AND ELSE 0 THEN
      WHILE 1+ REPEAT
      2DUP SWAP - 2 < 0= IF 2DUP SWAP ?DO DUP I CELLS FE-END + ! LOOP THEN SWAP DROP
    THEN
  REPEAT DROP ;
: REM ( e --- n ) DUP CELLS FE-END + @ SWAP - 16 MIN 0 MAX ;
: CMP ( x1 x2 --- n ) 2DUP < IF 2DROP -1 EXIT THEN > IF 1 ELSE 0 THEN ;
: KEY-CMP ( e1 e2 --- n )
  2DUP 7 FE@ SWAP 7 FE@ SWAP CMP ?DUP IF >R 2DROP R> EXIT THEN
  2DUP 8 FE@ SWAP 8 FE@ SWAP CMP ?DUP IF >R 2DROP R> EXIT THEN
  2 FE@ SWAP 2 FE@ SWAP CMP ;
VARIABLE SA  VARIABLE SB
: SEQ-CMP ( p q --- n )
\ Two positions' runs, operation by operation; then the shorter, then the earlier, first.
  SB ! SA !
  SA @ REM SB @ REM MIN 0 ?DO SA @ I + SB @ I + KEY-CMP ?DUP IF UNLOOP EXIT THEN LOOP
  SA @ REM SB @ REM CMP ?DUP IF EXIT THEN
  SA @ SB @ CMP ;
: LCP ( p q --- n )
  SB ! SA ! SA @ REM SB @ REM MIN 0 ?DO SA @ I + SB @ I + KEY-CMP IF I UNLOOP EXIT THEN LOOP
  SA @ REM SB @ REM MIN ;
CREATE FPOS #FE-MAX CELLS FACTOR? AND ALLOT  VARIABLE #FPOS
CREATE FTMP #FE-MAX CELLS FACTOR? AND ALLOT
CREATE FLCP #FE-MAX CELLS FACTOR? AND ALLOT
VARIABLE MS-W VARIABLE MS-LO VARIABLE MS-MID VARIABLE MS-HI VARIABLE MS-I VARIABLE MS-J VARIABLE MS-K
: P@ ( i --- p ) CELLS FPOS + @ ;
: MS-MERGE ( --- )
  MS-LO @ MS-I ! MS-MID @ MS-J ! MS-LO @ MS-K !
  BEGIN MS-K @ MS-HI @ < WHILE
    MS-I @ MS-MID @ < IF MS-J @ MS-HI @ < IF MS-I @ P@ MS-J @ P@ SEQ-CMP 0 > 0= ELSE -1 THEN ELSE 0 THEN
    IF MS-I @ P@ 1 MS-I +! ELSE MS-J @ P@ 1 MS-J +! THEN
    MS-K @ CELLS FTMP + !  1 MS-K +!
  REPEAT ;
: FAC-SORT ( --- )
\ Every position with room for a run, by its run (a bottom-up merge sort).
  1 MS-W !
  BEGIN MS-W @ #FPOS @ < WHILE
    0 BEGIN DUP #FPOS @ < WHILE
      DUP MS-LO !  DUP MS-W @ + #FPOS @ MIN MS-MID !  DUP MS-W @ 2* + #FPOS @ MIN MS-HI !
      MS-MERGE  MS-W @ 2* +
    REPEAT DROP
    FTMP FPOS #FPOS @ CELLS CMOVE  MS-W @ 2* MS-W !
  REPEAT ;
2048 CONSTANT #FC-MAX
CREATE FC #FC-MAX 4 * CELLS FACTOR? AND ALLOT  VARIABLE #FC  VARIABLE #FRUNS   \ [length][first in FPOS][members][bytes]
: FC# ( c --- a-addr ) 4 * CELLS FC + ;
: RUN-BYTES ( p n --- bytes ) 0 SWAP 0 ?DO OVER I + 3 FE@ + LOOP SWAP DROP ;
: RUN-RS? ( p n --- f )
\ Balanced, never below its own entry (rs_walk, strict).
  0 RS-D ! 0 ?DO DUP I + DUP 0 FE@ O-P = IF 1 FE@ RS-OP 0= IF DROP UNLOOP 0 EXIT THEN ELSE DROP THEN LOOP
  DROP RS-D @ 0= ;
: WORTH ( k bytes --- v ) DUP 2 - ROT * SWAP 1+ - ;
VARIABLE CL VARIABLE CS VARIABLE CN
: FC+ ( L s n --- )
\ A run of L operations, at FPOS s and the n-1 after it.
  CN ! CS ! CL !
  CS @ P@ CL @ 2DUP RUN-BYTES >R RUN-RS? R> SWAP OVER 2 > AND 0= IF DROP EXIT THEN
  1 #FRUNS +!
  CN @ OVER WORTH 0 > 0= IF DROP EXIT THEN
  #FC @ #FC-MAX < 0= ABORT" cross: too many runs to factor"
  #FC @ FC# >R CL @ R@ ! CS @ R@ CELL+ ! CN @ R@ 2 CELLS + ! R> 3 CELLS + ! 1 #FC +! ;
: FAC-RUNS ( --- )
\ Each run that recurs: at each length, the positions next in the order
\ sharing that many operations.
  0 #FC ! 0 #FRUNS !  #FPOS @ 2 < IF EXIT THEN
  #FPOS @ 1 ?DO I 1- P@ I P@ LCP I CELLS FLCP + ! LOOP
  17 2 ?DO
    0 #FPOS @ 1+ 1 ?DO
      I #FPOS @ < IF I CELLS FLCP + @ J < ELSE -1 THEN
      IF I OVER - 2 < 0= IF J OVER I OVER - FC+ THEN DROP I THEN
    LOOP DROP
  LOOP ;
CREATE TAKEN #FE-MAX FACTOR? AND ALLOT
CREATE MSORT 512 CELLS FACTOR? AND ALLOT
CREATE MEMB 512 CELLS FACTOR? AND ALLOT
VARIABLE FL  VARIABLE FLAST
: M@ ( j --- x ) CELLS MSORT + @ ;
: MSWAP ( j --- ) DUP M@ OVER 1- M@ ROT DUP >R CELLS MSORT + ! R> 1- CELLS MSORT + ! ;
: TAKEN? ( p --- f ) FL @ 0 ?DO DUP I + TAKEN + C@ IF DROP UNLOOP -1 EXIT THEN LOOP DROP 0 ;
: FREE-OF ( c --- k )
\ A candidate's positions free now, in order (layout.py's _free), in MEMB.
  FC# DUP @ FL !  DUP 2 CELLS + @ 512 MIN >R CELL+ @ CELLS FPOS + MSORT R@ CELLS CMOVE
  R@ 1 ?DO I BEGIN DUP 0 > IF DUP 1- M@ OVER M@ > ELSE 0 THEN WHILE DUP MSWAP 1- REPEAT DROP LOOP
  0 FLAST ! 0
  R> 0 ?DO
    I M@ DUP FLAST @ < OVER TAKEN? OR IF DROP ELSE DUP FL @ + FLAST ! OVER CELLS MEMB + ! 1+ THEN
  LOOP ;
CREATE FB-RUN #FB-MAX 2 * CELLS FACTOR? AND ALLOT  VARIABLE #FB 0 #FB !   \ a body: [first operation][length]
1024 CONSTANT #FU-MAX
CREATE FU #FU-MAX 4 * CELLS FACTOR? AND ALLOT  VARIABLE #FU 0 #FU !      \ a use: [ordinal][index][body][first operation]
VARIABLE BEST VARIABLE BESTV
: FAC-CHOOSE ( --- )
\ The best run by net bytes, over and over, until none pays (layout.py's
\ greedy pick; the first of equals here).
  TAKEN #FE @ 0 FILL  0 #FB ! 0 #FU !
  BEGIN
    -1 BEST ! 0 BESTV !
    #FC @ 0 ?DO I FREE-OF I FC# 3 CELLS + @ WORTH DUP BESTV @ > IF BESTV ! I BEST ! ELSE DROP THEN LOOP
  BEST @ 0< 0= WHILE
    BEST @ FREE-OF
    #FB @ #FB-MAX < 0= ABORT" cross: too many factored bodies"
    #FU @ OVER + #FU-MAX > ABORT" cross: too many factored uses"
    MEMB @ #FB @ 2* CELLS FB-RUN + !  FL @ #FB @ 2* 1+ CELLS FB-RUN + !
    0 ?DO
      I CELLS MEMB + @  FL @ 0 ?DO 1 OVER I + TAKEN + C! LOOP
      #FU @ 4 * CELLS FU + >R
      DUP 4 FE@ R@ !  DUP 5 FE@ R@ CELL+ !  #FB @ R@ 2 CELLS + !  R> 3 CELLS + !  1 #FU +!
    LOOP
    1 #FB +!
  REPEAT ;
: FAC-SEARCH ( --- )
  FAC-ON @ 0= IF EXIT THEN
  NOP-FILL RS-FILL
  #FE @ 0 ?DO I FE-KEY I FE-SAFE I 9 FE! LOOP
  FE-SEGS
  0 #FPOS ! #FE @ 0 ?DO I REM 2 < 0= IF I #FPOS @ CELLS FPOS + ! 1 #FPOS +! THEN LOOP
  FAC-SORT FAC-RUNS FAC-CHOOSE
  S" cross-cv8: factor - " TYPE #FB @ . S" bodies, " TYPE #FU @ . S" uses; " TYPE
  #FKEPT @ . S" words kept as hot, " TYPE #FRUNS @ . S" runs considered, " TYPE #FE @ . S" operations kept" TYPE CR ;

\ Pass 3.
CREATE FB-OPS #FB-MAX 64 * CELLS FACTOR? AND ALLOT   \ a body's operations, 16 at most, as this pass has them
VARIABLE UI VARIABLE UP VARIABLE UB VARIABLE UN VARIABLE UK VARIABLE FU-SAVED
: FU-SAME? ( j --- f )
  DUP UP @ + UK !  UI @ + OP-ID
  UK @ 2 FE@ = SWAP UK @ 1 FE@ = AND SWAP UK @ 0 FE@ = AND ;
: FU-APPLY ( u --- )
  4 * CELLS FU + DUP CELL+ @ UI !  DUP 2 CELLS + @ UB !  3 CELLS + @ UP !
  UB @ 2* 1+ CELLS FB-RUN + @ UN !
  UI @ UN @ + #OPS @ > ABORT" cross: a factored run past its word's end"
  UN @ 0 ?DO
    I FU-SAME? 0= ABORT" cross: a factored run changed between passes"
    I IF UI @ I + LTG + C@ ABORT" cross: a factored run is landed on" THEN
    UP @ I + 3 FE@ FU-SAVED +!
  LOOP
  UB @ FB-SNAP + C@ 0= IF
    UI @ OP# UB @ 64 * CELLS FB-OPS + UN @ 4 * CELLS CMOVE  1 UB @ FB-SNAP + C!
  THEN
  UN @ 1 ?DO UI @ I + KILL LOOP
  O-FB UB @ 0 0 UI @ OP!  0 CHAIN-SIZE NEGATE FU-SAVED +! ;
: FAC-APPLY ( --- )
\ Each use in this word a call to its body.
  PASS @ 3 < #FU @ 0= OR IF EXIT THEN
  LAST-SHADOW @ ORD LANDED
  #FU @ 0 ?DO I 4 * CELLS FU + @ OVER = IF I FU-APPLY THEN LOOP DROP COMPACT ;
VARIABLE FB-BYTES
: LAY-BODIES ( --- )
\ The bodies after the last word, [run][EXIT] (the EXIT folded, as
\ layout.py's fold_exit does), each one's chain made calls to it.
  FAC-ON @ 0= PASS @ 3 < OR IF EXIT THEN
  THERE FB-BYTES !
  #FB @ 0 ?DO
    I FB-SNAP + C@ 0= ABORT" cross: a factored body never used"
    THERE I CELLS FB-CHAIN + @ PATCH-CHAIN  CHAIN-END I CELLS FB-CHAIN + !
    CODE-START
    I 64 * CELLS FB-OPS + OPS  I 2* 1+ CELLS FB-RUN + @ DUP #OPS ! 4 * CELLS CMOVE
    1 0 P+ FOLD-PASS COMPACT
    COUNTING @ IF COUNT-SITES THEN
    THERE RELAX ENCODE 0 #OPS !
  LOOP
  THERE FB-BYTES @ - FB-BYTES !
  S" cross-cv8: factor - the words' code " TYPE FU-SAVED @ . S" bytes smaller, the bodies " TYPE FB-BYTES @ . CR ;
: FAC-RESET ( --- )
  FAC-ON @ 0= IF EXIT THEN
  #FB-MAX 0 ?DO CHAIN-END I CELLS FB-CHAIN + ! LOOP  FB-SNAP #FB-MAX 0 FILL  0 FU-SAVED !
  PASS @ 2 = IF 0 #FE ! 0 #FKEPT ! RSOK #ORD-MAX 0 FILL THEN ;

: END-DEF ( --- )
\ The definition's EXIT, the rewrites, the layout, the bytes - none for
\ a dead word; a callee's body kept first, the JIT's header if it has one.
  1 0 P+
  DEAD-NOW @ IF 0 #OPS ! 0 HS-ON ! 0 HS-STORE ! 0 HS-FINAL ! EXIT THEN
  HS-STORE @ ?DUP IF RAW-KEEP THEN  0 HS-ON ! 0 HS-STORE !
  FAC-ON @ PASS @ 2 = AND IF RS-KEEP THEN
  SPECIALISE COMPACT FOLD-PASS COMPACT PAIR-PASS COMPACT TEST-PASS COMPACT EQI-PASS COMPACT KEEP-PASS COMPACT
  FAC-ON @ IF PASS @ 2 = IF FAC-KEEP THEN FAC-APPLY THEN
  COUNTING @ IF COUNT-SITES THEN
  JH-NAMED? IF JH-PLAIN? ELSE 0 THEN IF
    THERE DUP X-JITDEAD IF 1+ ELSE 5 + THEN DUP RELAX #OPS @ ADDR SWAP -   ( xt len )
    DUP JIT-HEADER,  0 HS-FINAL !  ENCODE 0 #OPS !  JD-PAD,
  ELSE THERE RELAX  0 HS-FINAL !  ENCODE 0 #OPS ! THEN ;

\ ---- the shadows ----------------------------------------------------
VARIABLE IN-KERNEL 0 IN-KERNEL !   \ on while kernel.4 is compiled: rebinding is the kernel's uses only
: >REDIR ( shadow --- a-addr ) 9 CELLS + ;
: REF-T ( shadow-body --- )
\ What a target word's name does where the cross compiler meets it.
\ An X8 the kernel's X branches to is called as X - the latest code of
\ that name (the translator's --drop-x8) - except from a later X8 of
\ the same name, which defers to the one before it. Inside a definition
\ a target word is compiled, IMMEDIATE or not (cross.4's rule: only
\ TRANSIENT's words run).
\ The overlays are written for a running Forth, where an IMMEDIATE word
\ runs: met in one of their definitions it needs a twin in TRANSIENT.
  STATE-T @ IF
    IN-KERNEL @ 0= IF DUP 5 CELLS + @ IF ." cross: " DUP SH-NAME TYPE CR
      -1 ABORT" cross: an overlay's IMMEDIATE word with no twin" THEN THEN
    DUP >REDIR @ ?DUP IF LAST-SHADOW @ >REDIR @ OVER = IF DROP ELSE SWAP DROP THEN THEN
    DUP 8 CELLS + @ ?DUP IF SWAP DROP O-RB SWAP 0 0 OP+ EXIT THEN
    DUP CELL+ @
    DUP K-PRIM = IF DROP DUP 2 CELLS + @ SWAP P+ EXIT THEN
    DROP HS-TRY IF EXIT THEN DUP CELL+ @                \ a call the translator inlined
    DUP K-CONST = IF DROP 2 CELLS + @ LIT+ EXIT THEN
    K-DATA = IF >R O-DC R@ @ R@ @ >BODY-T R> OP+ EXIT THEN
    DUP 2 CELLS + @ ?DUP IF SWAP P+ EXIT THEN          \ tiny, format-10: its opcode
    DUP REF! >R O-C R@ @ 0 R> OP+ EXIT
  THEN
  DUP 4 CELLS + @ ?DUP IF SWAP DROP EXECUTE EXIT THEN
  DUP CELL+ @
  DUP K-DATA = IF DROP @ >BODY-T EXIT THEN
  K-CONST = IF 2 CELLS + @ EXIT THEN
  ." cross: no host action for " 3 CELLS + @ .TNAME CR
  -1 ABORT" cross: a target word met outside a definition" ;

VARIABLE HEADERLESS 0 HEADERLESS !
CREATE LAST-NAME 40 ALLOT
VARIABLE ALLOT-HOOK 0 ALLOT-HOOK !   \ what the next ALLOT-T does instead, or 0
: "HEADER ( --- host-action )
\ The shadow and the target header for the next name in the input - no
\ target header for the design's headerless words, or while HEADERLESS
\ is on (TLINK 0 then).
  0 ALLOT-HOOK !
  #SHADOWS @ #ORD-MAX < 0= ABORT" cross: too many words"
  #SHADOWS @ DEAD + C@ DEAD-NOW !
  >IN @ CREATE >IN !
  BL WORD COUNT DUP LAST-NAME C! 2DUP LAST-NAME 1+ SWAP CMOVE
  2DUP INTERP-XT >R
  2DUP G-HEADERLESS LIST-INDEX 0< 0= HEADERLESS @ OR DEAD-NOW @ OR IF 2DROP 0 TLINK ! ELSE NAME,-T THEN R> ;

VARIABLE SH-KIND
: SHADOW, ( kind value host-action --- )
\ The shadow's fields, right after "HEADER: [t-xt][kind][value][t-nfa]
\ [host action][immediate][test-branch long][short][rebind record]
\ [redirect: X's shadow for an X8 it replaces][hot call][ordinal][calls
\ pending][pending: X until its place][POSTPONEd cells pending][name].
\ A rebind record for the kernel's primitives of the rebound names.
  >R >R DUP SH-KIND ! HERE LAST-SHADOW ! THERE , , R> , TLINK @ , R> , 0 ,
  LAST-NAME COUNT TEST-OPS SWAP , ,
  IN-KERNEL @ SH-KIND @ K-PRIM = AND IF LAST-NAME COUNT RB-OF ELSE 0 THEN ,
  0 , #SHADOWS @ HOT-CODE , #SHADOWS @ ,  CHAIN-END , 0 , 0 ,
  LAST-NAME COUNT DUP C, HERE SWAP DUP ALLOT CMOVE ALIGN
  LAST-SHADOW @ #SHADOWS @ CELLS ORD-SH + !
  1 #SHADOWS +! ;

: DATA-HEADER ( --- )
\ A data word: [DOVAR][3 bytes, 4 under the tag][aligned parameter field]
\ (cv8.4's and cv8t.4's CREATE8, CV8-DOES-RESERVE 3 or 4).
  "HEADER >R K-DATA 0 R> SHADOW,
  69 OP,-T 0 C,-T 0 C,-T 0 C,-T G-TAG2 IF 0 C,-T THEN ALIGN-T ;

\ The host actions: what a target word does when the cross compiler meets
\ it outside a definition - the overlays build tables and set variables
\ while they load.
: I-! !-T ;
: I-C! C!-T ;
: I-@ @-T ;
: I-C@ C@-T ;
: I-, ,-T ;
: I-C, C,-T ;
: I-ALLOT ALLOT-T ;
: I-FILL ( t-addr u c --- )   \ 714: cv8-fuse-inline.4 zeroes INL-OPS so
  SWAP 0 ?DO OVER I + OVER SWAP C!-T LOOP 2DROP ;
: I-ALIGN ALIGN-T ;
: I-CELLS CELLS-T ;
: I-CHARS ;
: I-' ( "name" --- t-xt )
  BL WORD COUNT T-SHADOW 0= ABORT" cross: ' of no target word"
  DUP PENDING? ABORT" cross: ' of a word not placed yet" DUP REF! @ ;
: I->OP C@-T ;      \ a CV8 primitive's body starts with its opcode
: I-HERE THERE ;
: I-FOLD-DEFAULTS ( --- )
\ cv8-fuse.4's copy of FOLD-OPS into FOLD-TABLE, done in the image.
  S" FOLD-OPS" T-SHADOW 0= ABORT" cross: no FOLD-OPS" @ >BODY-T
  S" #FOLD-OPS" T-SHADOW 0= ABORT" cross: no #FOLD-OPS" 2 CELLS + @
  0 ?DO DUP I + C@-T C,-T LOOP DROP ;
: I-CV8-SHIFT-DEFAULT TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ 8 = IF 3 ELSE 2 THEN ;
: I-CREATE ( "name" --- ) DATA-HEADER DOES> REF-T ;

\ PART 6: THE CV8 COMPILER IN KERNEL.4'S PLACE. Each kernel.4 word whose
\ X8 an overlay defines - its compiler words, cv8b.4's header words,
\ kfast's search - has the last X8's code: the translator's swap (tools/
\ layout.py --cv8-compiler) made while compiling. kernel.4's X waits, its
\ body skipped - no header and no code; a call to it is chained, and so
\ is a cell POSTPONE lays down for it - and at the last X8 its header is
\ laid down, the X8's code following it is its code, and what waited on
\ it is made. (A header a little later in the dictionary than kernel.4's
\ place for it: X is defined once, so nothing finds another.) The
\ sources are read first for their X8 names and how many of each.

CREATE SWAPS 1024 ALLOT  VARIABLE #SWAPS 0 #SWAPS !
CREATE X8-TOTAL 128 ALLOT  X8-TOTAL 128 0 FILL   \ each X's X8 definitions in the sources
CREATE X8-SEEN 128 ALLOT                          \ ...and so far, this pass
: SWAP-SET ( --- c-addr u ) SWAPS #SWAPS @ ;
: SWAP-ADD ( c-addr u --- )
  2DUP SWAP-SET LIST-INDEX DUP 0< 0= IF >R 2DROP R> ELSE DROP
    DUP 1+ #SWAPS @ + 1024 > ABORT" cross: too many X8 words"
    >R SWAPS #SWAPS @ + R@ CMOVE R> #SWAPS +! 32 SWAPS #SWAPS @ + C! 1 #SWAPS +!
    SWAP-SET LIST-COUNT 1-
  THEN
  DUP 128 < 0= ABORT" cross: too many X8 words"
  X8-TOTAL + DUP C@ 1+ SWAP C! ;
CREATE LINEBUF 260 ALLOT  VARIABLE SCAN-FID
: FIRST-TOKEN ( c-addr u --- c-addr len )
  0 BEGIN 2DUP > IF 2 PICK OVER + C@ 32 > ELSE 0 THEN WHILE 1+ REPEAT SWAP DROP ;
: X8-NAME? ( c-addr u --- f ) DUP 1 > IF + 1- C@ 56 = ELSE 2DROP 0 THEN ;
: OPB-SET ( --- c-addr u )
  G-OP-BODIES IF S" FILL CMOVE SCAN SKIP (PARSE) HASH PLACE (FIND) (>NUMBER) THREAD-FIND +! ?DUP 2@ 2! > 0= "
  ELSE S" FILL CMOVE SCAN SKIP (PARSE) HASH PLACE " THEN ;
\ The op-body words in kernel.4's order, and how many definitions each
\ has in kernel.4 and the overlays: only one defined once moves among
\ the primitives (--op-inline).
CREATE OPBS 512 ALLOT  VARIABLE #OPBS 0 #OPBS !
CREATE OPB-COUNTS 64 ALLOT  OPB-COUNTS 64 0 FILL
: OPB-LIST ( --- c-addr u ) OPBS #OPBS @ ;
: OPB-NOTE ( c-addr u --- )
  2DUP OPB-SET LIST-INDEX 0< IF 2DROP EXIT THEN
  2DUP OPB-LIST LIST-INDEX DUP 0< IF
    DROP DUP 1+ #OPBS @ + 512 > ABORT" cross: too many op-body words"
    >R OPBS #OPBS @ + R@ CMOVE R> #OPBS +! 32 OPBS #OPBS @ + C! 1 #OPBS +!
    OPB-LIST LIST-COUNT 1-
  ELSE >R 2DROP R> THEN
  OPB-COUNTS + DUP C@ 1+ SWAP C! ;
\ Iteration 736: G-TRIM8 - an overlay's NAME8 that is NAME (chainorder's LINK-LEN8, NEXT-NFA88: the translator gives
\ their bodies to NAME), the name in the source shortened as read; G-ONCE - a name only its first definition makes,
\ a later one skipped (cv8b.4's LINK-LEN and NEXT-NFA8 after chainorder's, loaded before cv8b.4).
CREATE ONCE-SEEN 32 ALLOT  CREATE ONCE-SCAN 32 ALLOT  ONCE-SCAN 32 0 FILL
: ONCE? ( c-addr u seen --- f )
  >R G-ONCE LIST-INDEX DUP 0< IF DROP R> DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  R> + DUP C@ IF DROP -1 EXIT THEN 1 SWAP C! 0 ;
: SRC-TOKEN-END ( u --- c-addr ) SOURCE DROP >IN @ + BEGIN DUP C@ BL = WHILE 1+ REPEAT + 1- ;
: SCAN-LINE ( u --- )
\ A line that starts ": X8 " adds X; one that defines an op-body word
\ counts it. A word of G-SKIP is not there (Iteration 736).
  DUP 3 < IF DROP EXIT THEN
  LINEBUF 2 S" : " COMPARE IF DROP EXIT THEN
  LINEBUF 2 + SWAP 2 - FIRST-TOKEN               ( c-addr len )
  2DUP G-SKIP LIST-INDEX 0< 0= IF 2DROP EXIT THEN
  2DUP G-TRIM8 LIST-INDEX 0< 0= IF 1- THEN          \ 736: chainorder's NAME8 takes NAME's place
  2DUP ONCE-SCAN ONCE? IF 2DROP EXIT THEN
  2DUP OPB-NOTE
  2DUP X8-NAME? IF 1- SWAP-ADD ELSE 2DROP THEN ;
: SCAN-FILE ( c-addr u --- )
  R/O OPEN-FILE ABORT" cross: can't open an overlay" SCAN-FID !
  BEGIN LINEBUF 256 SCAN-FID @ READ-LINE ABORT" cross: can't read an overlay" WHILE
    SCAN-LINE
  REPEAT DROP SCAN-FID @ CLOSE-FILE DROP ;
: SCAN-SOURCES ( --- )
  S" kernel.4" SCAN-FILE
  G-OVERLAYS LIST-COUNT 0 ?DO I G-OVERLAYS LIST-TOKEN SCAN-FILE LOOP ;

: NEXT-WORDS ( --- c-addr u ) S" [CHAR] CHAR ' ['] POSTPONE [COMPILE] " ;

: PLACE-X ( x-shadow --- )
\ X's header here, its code what follows; the calls and cells waiting on
\ it made, its IMMEDIATE (kernel.4's) on the header.
  >R R@ SH-NAME NAME,-T
  R@ 5 CELLS + @ IF TLINK @ DUP C@-T 64 OR SWAP C!-T THEN
  THERE R@ !  TLINK @ R@ 3 CELLS + !  0 R@ 13 CELLS + !
  R@ @ R@ 12 CELLS + @ PATCH-CHAIN
  R@ 14 CELLS + @ BEGIN ?DUP WHILE DUP @-T SWAP R@ @ OVER - SWAP !-T REPEAT
  R> DROP ;
: LAST-X8? ( x-shadow --- f )
\ The X8 being defined is the last of its name: X takes its place here.
  SH-NAME SWAP-SET LIST-INDEX DUP 0< ABORT" cross: an X8's X not in the swap set"     ( k )
  DUP X8-SEEN + DUP C@ 1+ SWAP C!
  DUP X8-SEEN + C@ SWAP X8-TOTAL + C@ = ;

: SKIP-DEF ( --- )
\ Past kernel.4's own body of a replaced word, to its ; - comments, a
\ string and a quoted next word skipped whole.
  BEGIN
    BL WORD DUP C@ 0= IF DROP REFILL 0= ABORT" cross: a replaced definition never ends"
    ELSE COUNT
      2DUP S" ;" COMPARE 0= IF 2DROP EXIT THEN
      2DUP S" \" COMPARE 0= IF SOURCE SWAP DROP >IN ! THEN
      2DUP S" (" COMPARE 0= IF 41 PARSE 2DROP THEN
      2DUP S" .(" COMPARE 0= IF 41 PARSE 2DROP THEN
      DUP 1 > IF 2DUP + 1- C@ 34 = IF 34 PARSE 2DROP THEN THEN
      2DUP NEXT-WORDS LIST-INDEX 0< 0= IF BL WORD DROP THEN
      2DROP
    THEN
  0 UNTIL ;

: CHECK-PLACED ( --- )
  #SHADOWS @ 0 ?DO
    I CELLS ORD-SH + @ DUP PENDING? IF ." cross: " SH-NAME TYPE CR -1 ABORT" cross: a replaced word never placed" THEN DROP
  LOOP ;

: X8-OF ( c-addr u --- shadow | 0 )
\ Is this an X8 whose body kernel.4's X branches to? Then X's shadow:
\ its own name is never looked up - the translator's --drop-x8 - and it
\ has no header, and its callers call X. AGAIN8, with no AGAIN in
\ kernel.4, keeps its name.
  2DUP X8-NAME? 0= IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  1- 2DUP SWAP-SET LIST-INDEX 0< IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  T-SHADOW 0= IF 0 THEN ;

\ The format-10 words whose bodies are their opcode and EXIT (tools/
\ layout.py's _OPB, --op-bodies), and placed among the primitives with
\ --op-inline, so that PRIMITIVE? takes them for primitives and the
\ run-time compiler copies their opcode.
: OPBODY-OP ( c-addr u --- op | 0 )
  2DUP OPB-SET LIST-INDEX 0< IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN OPS10-OF ;

\ The op-body words placed among the primitives (--op-inline): each is
\ made at (PRIMITIVES-END), its name taken from the list, and kernel.4's
\ own definition of it skipped when it comes.
CREATE INLS 512 ALLOT  VARIABLE #INLS 0 #INLS !
: INLINED? ( c-addr u --- f ) INLS #INLS @ LIST-INDEX 0< 0= ;
: INL-ADD ( c-addr u --- )
  DUP 1+ #INLS @ + 512 > ABORT" cross: too many inlined words"
  >R INLS #INLS @ + R@ CMOVE R> #INLS +! 32 INLS #INLS @ + C! 1 #INLS +! ;
VARIABLE OPINL-OP
: (OPINL) ( --- )
\ Never the JIT's header (--jitimg): below (PRIMITIVES-END) a word is a
\ primitive to COMPILE,8, which copies its first byte - the translator's
\ header there made (PARSE) the JIT's opcode (results/drafts/selfhost-
\ plan-666.md, phase 3).
  "HEADER >R K-COLON OPINL-OP @ R> SHADOW,
  DEAD-NOW @ 0= IF OPINL-OP @ OP,-T 1 OP,-T THEN
  DOES> REF-T ;
: OPINL ( c-addr u op --- )
\ The word named c-addr u, its body [op][EXIT]: the input is the name
\ while it is made.
  OPINL-OP ! 2DUP INL-ADD
  SRC @ >R #SRC @ >R >IN @ >R
  #SRC ! SRC ! 0 >IN !
  (OPINL)
  R> >IN ! R> #SRC ! R> SRC ! ;
: INLINE-OPBODIES ( --- )
  OPB-LIST LIST-COUNT 0 ?DO
    I OPB-COUNTS + C@ 1 = IF
      I OPB-LIST LIST-TOKEN 2DUP OPBODY-OP ?DUP IF OPINL ELSE 2DROP THEN
    THEN
  LOOP ;

\ A definition does not find itself until its ; (kernel.4's : and ;, a
\ HEADER revealed at the end) - file-sysc3.4's OPEN-FILE calls the one
\ before it. CREATE puts the shadow on its thread at once, so the
\ thread's head is put back, and REVEAL at ; puts the shadow there.
VARIABLE HID-CELL  VARIABLE HID-HEAD
: HIDE-NEXT ( --- )
  >IN @ BL WORD COUNT CURRENT @ @ HASH 1+ CELLS CURRENT @ +
  DUP HID-CELL ! @ HID-HEAD ! >IN ! ;
: UNREVEAL ( --- ) HID-HEAD @ HID-CELL @ ! ;

\ TIB, POCKET and INCLUDE-BUFFER past the image's end (the translator's
\ --bss): each a word that pushes START + its offset, the LIT32 patched
\ at the end, and the ALLOT after it counted there, not here.
: BSS-SET ( --- c-addr u ) S" TIB POCKET INCLUDE-BUFFER " ;
CREATE BSSR 8 CELLS ALLOT  VARIABLE #BSS 0 #BSS !    \ [LIT32's operand][bytes]
: BSS-ALLOT ( n --- ) #BSS @ 1- 2 * CELLS BSSR + CELL+ +! ;
: BSS-WORD ( --- )
  "HEADER >R K-COLON 0 R> SHADOW,
  CODE-START
  O-LIT32 0 0 0 OP+
  S" START" T-SHADOW 0= ABORT" cross: no START" DUP REF! >R O-C R@ @ 0 R> OP+
  S" @" NAME-OP 0 P+  S" +" NAME-OP 0 P+  1 0 P+
  COUNTING @ IF COUNT-SITES THEN
  THERE RELAX ENCODE 0 #OPS !
  LIT32-AT @ #BSS @ 2 * CELLS BSSR + !  1 CELLS-T #BSS @ 2 * CELLS BSSR + CELL+ !
  1 #BSS +!
  ['] BSS-ALLOT ALLOT-HOOK ! ;
: BSS-PLACE ( --- t-addr )
\ The buffers' offsets into their LIT32s; the end of the last.
  THERE ALIGNED-T
  #BSS @ 0 ?DO
    DUP I 2 * CELLS BSSR + @ 2DUP W!-T 2 + SWAP 16 RSHIFT SWAP W!-T
    I 2 * CELLS BSSR + CELL+ @ ALIGNED-T +
  LOOP ;

\ FORTH-WORDLIST's body is its count and the design's G-THREADS heads
\ (the translator's --threads): kernel.4 allots 32.
: WL-ALLOT ( n --- ) DROP #TTHREADS CELLS-T ALLOT-T ;

\ The kinds of : definition.
VARIABLE COLON-OP   VARIABLE SWAP-K   VARIABLE OPB-K   VARIABLE REDIR-K
: COLON-VALUE ( c-addr u --- n )
\ The opcode a word's calls become, or 0: a format-10 operation's
\ (tools/sod16.py's ops10_rewrite - first, as opcode_L reads it; each is
\ defined once, in kernel.4 or an overlay), a kernel tiny word's
\ (specialisation tiny).
  2DUP OPS10-OF ?DUP IF
    >R T-SHADOW IF 2 CELLS + @ R@ = ABORT" cross: a format-10 word defined twice" THEN R> EXIT THEN
  IN-KERNEL @ 0= IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  8 SPEC? 0= IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  TINY-SET LIST-INDEX DUP 0< IF DROP 0 ELSE TINY-BASE + THEN ;

VARIABLE NEXT-OP 0 NEXT-OP !     \ The next primitive's opcode.
VARIABLE NEXT-ESC 0 NEXT-ESC !   \ ...and the next escaped one's selector (--escape)
: ESCAPED? ( c-addr u --- f ) G-ESCAPE IF G-ESC-PRIMS LIST-INDEX 0< 0= ELSE 2DROP 0 THEN ;
: OPCODE-T ( c-addr u --- op )
\ The next primitive's opcode, by kernel.4's order: an escaped one's
\ selector + 256 (two bytes, ESC and the selector), the others closing up
\ (tools/sod16.py's cv8_op).
  ESCAPED? IF NEXT-ESC @ 256 + 1 NEXT-ESC +! ELSE NEXT-OP @ 1 NEXT-OP +! THEN ;
VARIABLE PRIM-OP-NOW

: REDIRECTED ( shadow --- shadow' )
\ An X8 the kernel's X branches to is reached as X, but from a later X8
\ of its own name (REF-T).
  DUP >REDIR @ ?DUP IF LAST-SHADOW @ >REDIR @ OVER = IF DROP ELSE SWAP DROP THEN THEN ;

: OPC-NAMES ( --- c-addr u ) S" EXIT-OP LIT16-OP BRANCH-OP 0BRANCH-OP LIT32-OP DOVAR-OP DODOES-OP LIT8-OP LIT64-OP " ;
: T2-CONST ( x c-addr u --- x' )
\ cv8t.4's opcode constants in this design's codes (layout.py's _cn and
\ _cx): a fixed operation's one-byte code; the short branches' and the
\ JIT's code, or 0 where the design has none.
  G-TAG2 0= IF 2DROP EXIT THEN
  2DUP OPC-NAMES LIST-INDEX 0< 0= IF 2DROP T2C DUP 0= ABORT" cross: an opcode constant escaped" EXIT THEN
  2DUP S" BRANCH8-OP" COMPARE 0= IF 2DROP DROP S" BRANCH8" OPS10-OF T2C EXIT THEN
  2DUP S" ?BRANCH8-OP" COMPARE 0= IF 2DROP DROP S" ?BRANCH8" OPS10-OF T2C EXIT THEN
  2DUP S" JIT-OP" COMPARE 0= IF 2DROP DROP G-JIT IF 65533 T2C ELSE 0 THEN EXIT THEN
  2DROP ;

ONLY FORTH ALSO TRANSIENT DEFINITIONS FORTH

: PRIMITIVE ( --- )
\ The next opcode: a body of the opcode and EXIT, the macro bit (32) set
\ as the cell cross compiler set it; COMPILE, asks PRIMITIVE? by address.
\ A fold-set primitive's folded opcode is FOLD-BASE + its place.
  >IN @ >R BL WORD COUNT 2DUP OPCODE-T PRIM-OP-NOW !
  2DUP G-FOLDS LIST-INDEX >R SPECIAL-SET LIST-INDEX R> R> >IN !
  DUP 0< 0= IF FOLD-BASE + PRIM-OP-NOW @ CHARS FOLDMAP + C! ELSE DROP THEN
  DUP 0< 0= IF CELLS SPECIAL-OPS + PRIM-OP-NOW @ SWAP ! ELSE DROP THEN
  "HEADER >R
  TLINK @ ?DUP IF DUP C@-T 32 OR SWAP C!-T THEN
  K-PRIM PRIM-OP-NOW @ R> SHADOW,
  DEAD-NOW @ 0= IF
    PRIM-OP-NOW @ OP,-T 1 OP,-T
  THEN
  DOES> REF-T ;

: PRIMITIVE-SLOT ( --- )
\ An opcode kept without a name (kernel.4, Iteration 147) - or, escaped,
\ a selector.
  BL WORD COUNT OPCODE-T DROP ;

: : ( --- )
\ A kernel word an overlay's X8 replaces: it waits for the last X8, its
\ own body skipped (PART 6). An X8 of it: no header of its own - the last
\ one X's. An op-body word: [op][EXIT], its body skipped - or nothing
\ here at all, made among the primitives. Any other: its operations, to ;.
  >IN @ >R BL WORD COUNT R> >IN !                      ( c-addr u )
  2DUP INLINED? IF 2DROP BL WORD DROP SKIP-DEF EXIT THEN
  2DUP G-SKIP LIST-INDEX 0< 0= IF 2DROP BL WORD DROP SKIP-DEF EXIT THEN   \ 736: G-SKIP - the translator drops it
  2DUP G-TRIM8 LIST-INDEX 0< 0= IF DUP SRC-TOKEN-END BL SWAP C! 1- THEN   \ 736: G-TRIM8, G-ONCE
  2DUP ONCE-SEEN ONCE? IF 2DROP BL WORD DROP SKIP-DEF EXIT THEN
  2DUP HS-FNAME PLACE  -1 HS-FINAL !
  2DUP COLON-VALUE COLON-OP !
  IN-KERNEL @ IF 2DUP SWAP-SET LIST-INDEX ELSE -1 THEN SWAP-K !
  2DUP OPBODY-OP OPB-K !
  X8-OF DUP REDIR-K ! 0= 0= HEADERLESS !
  SWAP-K @ 0< 0= IF -1 HEADERLESS ! THEN
  SWAP-K @ 0< OPB-K @ 0= AND IF HIDE-NEXT THEN
  "HEADER >R
  REDIR-K @ ?DUP IF
    DUP PENDING? 0= ABORT" cross: an X8 after its X took its place"
    DUP LAST-X8? IF DUP SH-NAME HS-FNAME PLACE PLACE-X ELSE DROP 0 HS-FINAL ! THEN
  THEN
  K-COLON COLON-OP @ R> SHADOW,  0 HEADERLESS !
  REDIR-K @ LAST-SHADOW @ >REDIR !
  SWAP-K @ 0< 0= IF -1 LAST-SHADOW @ 13 CELLS + ! 0 HS-FINAL ! SKIP-DEF ELSE
    OPB-K @ IF
      DEAD-NOW @ 0= IF THERE OPB-K @ OPSIZE-T 1+ DUP JH-OPB >R OPB-K @ OP,-T 1 OP,-T R> IF JD-PAD, ELSE 2DROP THEN THEN
      0 HS-FINAL ! SKIP-DEF
    ELSE
      REDIR-K @ ?DUP 0= IF LAST-SHADOW @ THEN HS-BEGIN UNREVEAL CODE-START !CSP T]
    THEN
  THEN
  DOES> REF-T ;

: ; ( --- ) END-DEF T[ ?CSP REVEAL ;

: IMMEDIATE ( --- )
  TLINK @ ?DUP IF DUP C@-T 64 OR SWAP C!-T THEN
  -1 LAST-SHADOW @ 5 CELLS + ! ;

: VARIABLE ( --- )
\ A data word - but (PRIMITIVES-END) first has the inlined op-body words
\ before it, the buffers are words past the image, and FORTH-WORDLIST
\ has the design's threads.
  >IN @ >R BL WORD COUNT R> >IN !
  2DUP S" (PRIMITIVES-END)" COMPARE 0= G-OP-INLINE AND IF INLINE-OPBODIES THEN
  2DUP BSS-SET LIST-INDEX 0< 0= G-BSS AND IF 2DROP BSS-WORD ELSE
    S" FORTH-WORDLIST" COMPARE 0= >R
    DATA-HEADER 0 ,-T
    R> IF ['] WL-ALLOT ALLOT-HOOK ! THEN
  THEN
  DOES> REF-T ;

: CONSTANT ( x --- )
  >IN @ >R BL WORD COUNT R> >IN ! T2-CONST
  "HEADER >R K-CONST OVER R> SHADOW, CODE-START LIT+ 0 HS-FINAL ! 0 HS-STORE ! END-DEF
  DOES> REF-T ;

: ALLOT-T ( n --- ) ALLOT-HOOK @ ?DUP IF 0 ALLOT-HOOK ! EXECUTE ELSE ALLOT-T THEN ;

: BEGIN ( --- j ) #OPS @ DUP MARK ;
: UNTIL ( j --- ) 4 QBR8-OP BR+ ;
: AGAIN ( j --- ) 3 BR8-OP BR+ ;
: IF ( --- j ) 4 QBR8-OP >FWD-BR ;
: THEN ( j --- ) >RESOLVE ;
: ELSE ( j1 --- j2 ) 3 BR8-OP >FWD-BR SWAP >RESOLVE ;
: WHILE ( j1 --- j2 j1 ) 4 QBR8-OP >FWD-BR SWAP ;
: REPEAT ( j1 j2 --- ) 3 BR8-OP BR+ >RESOLVE ;

FORWARD (DO)
FORWARD (LOOP)
FORWARD (.")
FORWARD (ABORT")
FORWARD (POSTPONE)

: DO ( --- j ) [ TRANSIENT ] (DO) [ FORTH ] #OPS @ DUP MARK ;
: LOOP-OP ( j --- )
\ (LOOP) and the cell after it - or (LOOP)'s format-10 opcode with a
\ branch's offset, where the design has it (ops10_rewrite's LOOPKIND).
  [ TRANSIENT ] ['] (LOOP) [ FORTH ] >BODY DUP FWD-SHADOW ?DUP IF
    DUP CELL+ @ K-COLON = OVER 2 CELLS + @ AND IF 2 CELLS + @ SWAP DROP 0 BR+ EXIT THEN DROP
  THEN FWD-REF >R O-LOOPC R> ROT 0 OP+ ;
\ Iteration 714: ?DO, for cv8-fuse-inline.4 (the gene rtinline) - (?DO)'s
\ format-10 opcode, a branch past the loop's end as the translator lays
\ it (sod16.py's LOOPKIND: QDO); its LOOP resolves it (-2 marks a ?DO's).
: ?DO ( --- j-skip j -2 )
  S" (?DO)" OPS10-OF DUP 0= ABORT" cross: not yet: ?DO without (?DO)'s format-10 opcode"
  0 >FWD-BR #OPS @ DUP MARK -2 ;
: LOOP ( j --- | j-skip j -2 --- )
  DUP -2 = IF DROP [ TRANSIENT ] LOOP-OP [ FORTH ] >RESOLVE EXIT THEN [ TRANSIENT ] LOOP-OP [ FORTH ] ;
: ." [ TRANSIENT ] (.") [ FORTH ] 34 PARSE STR+ ;
: ABORT" ( "ccc<quote>" --- )
\ (ABORT") and its string. Under the gene abortif (GUARD-ABORT?) the
\ translator's guard_aborts: ?BRANCH past the string and -1 before the
\ call, so a false flag skips it - except after a literal -1, where the
\ call always aborts. (Its other exception, a word with a DOES> tail
\ inside, cannot arise: no target definition here has one.) A branch to
\ the site lands on the guard, as there.
  GUARD-ABORT? IF
    #OPS @ DUP IF 1- DUP OP-K O-LIT = SWAP OP-A -1 = AND ELSE DROP 0 THEN
    0= IF
      4 QBR8-OP >FWD-BR -1 LIT+
      [ TRANSIENT ] (ABORT") [ FORTH ] 34 PARSE STR+ >RESOLVE EXIT
    THEN
  THEN
  [ TRANSIENT ] (ABORT") [ FORTH ] 34 PARSE STR+ ;
: POSTPONE ( "name" --- )
  BL WORD COUNT T-SHADOW 0= ABORT" cross: POSTPONE of no target word"
  REDIRECTED DUP REF!
  DUP 5 CELLS + @ IF >R O-C R@ @ 0 R> OP+ EXIT THEN
  >R O-PPC [ TRANSIENT ] ['] (POSTPONE) [ FORTH ] >BODY FWD-REF R@ @ R> OP+ ;
: ['] BL WORD COUNT T-SHADOW 0= ABORT" cross: ['] of no target word" REDIRECTED
  DUP PENDING? ABORT" cross: ['] of a word not placed yet" DUP REF! @ ALIT+ ;

: \ POSTPONE \ ; IMMEDIATE
: ( POSTPONE ( ; IMMEDIATE
: CHARS-T CHARS-T ;
: CELLS-T CELLS-T ;
: CELLBYTES-TOK TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ LIT+ ;
: CELLSHIFT-TOK TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ 4 = IF 2 ELSE 3 THEN LIT+ ;
: SIGNSHIFT-TOK TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ 8 * 1- LIT+ ;

\ PART 0's boot vectors: calls to COLD and WARM, then three cells, the
\ first word at 5 cells as the translator laid it.
FORWARD COLD
FORWARD WARM
FORWARD THROW
: DIV-EX ( --- ) 2 CELLS-T THERE - ALLOT-T -1 ,-T ;
: BREAK-EX ( --- ) -1 ,-T ;
: TIMER-EX ( --- ) -1 ,-T ;

FORTH DEFINITIONS

\ PART 8: THE CROSS COMPILER ITSELF.

VARIABLE DPL
: NUMBER? ( c-addr ---- d f)
  -1 DPL !
  BASE @ >R
  COUNT
  OVER C@ 45 = DUP >R IF 1 - SWAP 1 + SWAP THEN \ Get any - sign
  OVER C@ 36 = IF 16 BASE ! 1 - SWAP 1 + SWAP THEN   \ $ sign for hex.
  OVER C@ 35 = IF 10 BASE ! 1 - SWAP 1 + SWAP THEN   \ # sign for decimal
  DUP  0 > 0= IF  R> DROP R> BASE ! 0 EXIT THEN   \ Length 0 or less?
  >R >R 0 0 R> R>
  BEGIN
   >NUMBER
   DUP IF OVER C@ 46 = IF 1 - DUP DPL ! SWAP 1 + SWAP ELSE \ handle point.
         R> DROP R> BASE ! 0 EXIT THEN   \ Error if anything but point
       THEN
  DUP 0= UNTIL DROP DROP R> IF DNEGATE THEN
  R> BASE ! -1
;

: CALL-LIMIT ( n --- n' )
\ The wide tag has no three-byte call: cv8t.4's CALL, takes four bytes
\ past 16 KB, not 4 MB (layout.py patches its literal the same way).
  G-T2WIDE IF DUP 4194304 = IF LAST-NAME COUNT S" CALL," COMPARE 0= IF DROP 16384 THEN THEN THEN ;
: XWORD ( c-addr --- )
\ One word: a target or TRANSIENT word executes, a number is a literal
\ inside a definition and stays on the host stack outside one.
  FIND IF EXECUTE EXIT THEN
  DUP >R NUMBER? 0= IF R> COUNT TYPE ."  ?" CR -1 ABORT" cross: undefined word" THEN
  R> DROP DROP STATE-T @ IF CALL-LIMIT LIT+ THEN ;

: CROSS-COMPILE ( --- )
\ Cross-compile the rest of the input: to END-CROSS, or to the end of
\ the file being cross-included.
  ONLY TARGET DEFINITIONS ALSO TRANSIENT
  BEGIN
    BL WORD DUP C@ 0= IF
      DROP REFILL 0= IF ONLY FORTH ALSO DEFINITIONS EXIT THEN
    ELSE
      DUP COUNT S" END-CROSS" COMPARE 0= IF DROP ONLY FORTH ALSO DEFINITIONS EXIT THEN
      XWORD
    THEN
  0 UNTIL ;

: XINCLUDED ( c-addr u --- )
\ Cross-compile a whole file - kernel.4's INCLUDED with CROSS-COMPILE in
\ INTERPRET's place.
  R/O OPEN-FILE ABORT" cross: can't open a file" DUP >R
  INCLUDE-POINTER @ >R SID @ >R SRC @ >R #SRC @ >R >IN @ >R
  #SRC @ INCLUDE-POINTER +! INCLUDE-POINTER @ SRC !
  SID ! 0 #SRC ! 0 >IN !
  CROSS-COMPILE
  R> >IN ! R> #SRC ! R> SRC ! R> SID ! R> INCLUDE-POINTER !
  R> CLOSE-FILE DROP ;

: XINCLUDE-OVERLAYS ( --- )
  G-OVERLAYS LIST-COUNT 0 ?DO
    I G-OVERLAYS LIST-TOKEN 2DUP XINCLUDED
    PASS @ 3 = IF S" cross-cv8: " TYPE TYPE S"  to " TYPE THERE . CR ELSE 2DROP THEN
  LOOP ;

\ The run-time compiler's tables in this design's opcodes, as the
\ translator writes them (tools/layout.py, the compiler's own tables):
\ cv8.4's FOLD-OPS, the design's folds in fold-opcode order, padded with
\ 255.
: TXT ( c-addr u --- t-xt ) T-SHADOW 0= ABORT" cross: no such target word" @ ;

\ cv8-fuse.4's FOLD-TABLE always (the count, then the folds' opcodes);
\ with --rtfuse its SUPER-TABLE (the fused tests the compiler can make -
\ I + as I+ first - then the pairs, by opcode, to 24 entries; else none),
\ cv8-fuse-imm.4's IMM-OPS, and cv8-fuse-loopall.4's LOOPTAB (the eight
\ loop opcodes, I's offset, J's and UNLOOP's distance past it).
\ Under the two-bit tag the tables hold this design's one-byte codes: an
\ escaped operation cannot sit in a byte, so its entry goes (0, none);
\ the run-time folds go entirely - their opcode was the fold base plus a
\ place, which the ranking undoes (layout.py).
: TB! ( c t-addr --- t-addr+1 ) SWAP OVER C!-T 1+ ;
: T2-BYTES ( t-addr n --- ) 0 ?DO DUP I + DUP C@-T T2C SWAP C!-T LOOP DROP ;
: FOLD-TABLE! ( --- )
  S" FOLD-TABLE" T-SHADOW 0= IF EXIT THEN @ >BODY-T
  G-TAG2 IF 0 SWAP C!-T EXIT THEN
  G-FOLDS LIST-COUNT SWAP TB!
  G-FOLDS LIST-COUNT 0 ?DO I G-FOLDS LIST-TOKEN NAME-OP SWAP TB! LOOP DROP ;
: PRIM-OP ( c-addr u --- op | -1 )
\ A primitive's opcode (tools/sod16.py's cv8_op), or -1.
  T-SHADOW IF DUP CELL+ @ K-PRIM = IF 2 CELLS + @ ELSE DROP -1 THEN ELSE -1 THEN ;
: RT-TESTS ( --- c-addr u ) S" 0= < = U< - <> > 0< DUP OVER " ;
VARIABLE ST-AT  VARIABLE ST-N
: ST3 ( a b c --- ) ST-AT @ 2 + C!-T ST-AT @ 1+ C!-T ST-AT @ C!-T 3 ST-AT +! 1 ST-N +! ;
: SUPER-TABLE! ( --- )
  S" SUPER-TABLE" T-SHADOW 0= IF EXIT THEN @ >BODY-T DUP 1+ ST-AT ! 0 ST-N !
  G-RTFUSE IF
    S" I+" OPS10-OF ?DUP IF S" I" OPS10-OF ?DUP IF S" +" PRIM-OP ROT ST3 ELSE DROP THEN THEN
    RT-TESTS LIST-COUNT 0 ?DO
      I RT-TESTS LIST-TOKEN 2DUP TEST-OPS DROP ?DUP IF
        >R PRIM-OP DUP 0< IF DROP R> DROP ELSE S" ?BRANCH" PRIM-OP R> ST3 THEN
      ELSE 2DROP THEN
    LOOP
    PAIRS-INIT #PAIRS @ 0 ?DO
      ST-N @ 24 < IF I 3 * CELLS PAIRS + DUP @ OVER CELL+ @ ROT 2 CELLS + @ ST3 THEN
    LOOP
  THEN
  G-TAG2 IF                                   \ the entries in codes, the escaped ones out
    DUP 1+ ST-AT ! ST-N @ 0 ST-N ! 0 ?DO
      DUP 1+ I 3 * + DUP C@-T T2C OVER 1+ C@-T T2C ROT 2 + C@-T T2C
      2 PICK 0= 2 PICK 0= OR OVER 0= OR IF DROP 2DROP ELSE ST3 THEN
    LOOP
  THEN
  ST-N @ SWAP C!-T ;
: IMM-OPS! ( --- )
  S" IMM-OPS" T-SHADOW 0= IF EXIT THEN @ >BODY-T
  G-RTFUSE 2 SPEC? AND IF 120 ELSE 0 THEN SWAP TB!
  G-RTFUSE IF S" SWAP+I" OPS10-OF ELSE 0 THEN SWAP TB!
  S" +" PRIM-OP SWAP TB!  S" SWAP" PRIM-OP SWAP TB!
  G-RTFUSE IF S" DUP+I" OPS10-OF ELSE 0 THEN SWAP TB!
  G-RTFUSE IF S" DUP<I" OPS10-OF ELSE 0 THEN SWAP TB!
  S" DUP" PRIM-OP SWAP TB!  S" <" PRIM-OP SWAP TB!
  G-TAG2 IF 8 - 8 T2-BYTES ELSE DROP THEN ;
VARIABLE LT-AT
: NEAR-I? ( n --- f ) DUP 0 > SWAP 256 < AND ;
: LOOPTAB! ( --- )
  S" LOOPTAB" T-SHADOW 0= IF EXIT THEN @ >BODY-T LT-AT !
  8 0 DO
    I S" (DO) (LOOP) (+LOOP) (?DO) (LEAVE) I J UNLOOP " LIST-TOKEN OPS10-OF
    DUP 0= ABORT" cross: LOOPTAB needs all eight loop opcodes"
    G-TAG2 IF T2C DUP 0= ABORT" cross: LOOPTAB: a loop opcode escaped" THEN
    LT-AT @ I + C!-T
  LOOP
  S" I" TXT DUP 65536 < 0= ABORT" cross: LOOPTAB: I beyond 64 KB"
  DUP 255 AND LT-AT @ 8 + C!-T  DUP 8 RSHIFT LT-AT @ 9 + C!-T
  S" J" TXT OVER - DUP NEAR-I? 0= ABORT" cross: LOOPTAB: J not near I" LT-AT @ 10 + C!-T
  S" UNLOOP" TXT SWAP - DUP NEAR-I? 0= ABORT" cross: LOOPTAB: UNLOOP not near I" LT-AT @ 11 + C!-T ;
: FOLD-OPS! ( --- )
  S" FOLD-OPS" T-SHADOW 0= IF EXIT THEN @ >BODY-T
  23 0 DO 255 OVER I + C!-T LOOP
  G-TAG2 IF DROP EXIT THEN
  G-FOLDS LIST-COUNT 23 > ABORT" cross: more folds than FOLD-OPS holds"
  G-FOLDS LIST-COUNT 0 ?DO
    I G-FOLDS LIST-TOKEN NAME-OP DUP 0< ABORT" cross: a fold of no primitive"
    OVER I + C!-T
  LOOP DROP ;

\ Iteration 714 (self-hosting phase 6): cv8-fuse-var.4's VAR-OPS and
\ cv8-fuse-inline.4's INL-OPS, byte for byte as tools/layout.py writes
\ them - before, both stayed zeros here and the run-time fusions (the genes
\ rtvar and rtinline) were off in every self-built image (697). An
\ operation's names are sod16.py's t2_names: later kinds name over earlier
\ ones - the primitives, the fixed operations, the specialisations, the
\ folds (name;EXIT), the pairs ("A B"), the format-10 operations.
: BYTE-OF ( op --- code -1 | 0 )
\ The operation's one-byte code where it has one (layout.py's _byte); -1
\ (no such operation) has none.
  DUP 0< IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  G-TAG2 IF
    DUP 65533 = IF DROP T2JIT @ DUP 0< IF DROP 0 ELSE -1 THEN EXIT THEN
    >L2 DUP 256 < IF T2ONE + C@ DUP IF 1- -1 ELSE DROP 0 THEN ELSE DROP 0 THEN EXIT
  THEN
  DUP 128 < IF -1 ELSE DROP 0 THEN ;
: SPEC-OP ( c-addr u --- op | -1 )
\ A specialisation's opcode by its t2_names name - named whenever the
\ design has any (G-SPEC), as sod16.py names them.
  G-SPEC 0= IF 2DROP -1 EXIT THEN
  2DUP S" lit0 lit1 litm1 vf vs LSAVE LRESTORE L! LZERO " LIST-INDEX DUP 0< 0= IF SWAP DROP SWAP DROP 96 + EXIT THEN DROP
  2DUP TINY-SET LIST-INDEX DUP 0< 0= IF SWAP DROP SWAP DROP TINY-BASE + EXIT THEN DROP
  S" ADDI ADDIX EQI EQIX " LIST-INDEX DUP 0< 0= IF 120 + THEN ;
: FIXED-OP ( c-addr u --- op | -1 )
  S" LIT32 68 DOVAR 69 DODOES 70 LIT8 71 LIT8X 72 LIT64 124 " LIST-VALUE ;
: LAST-OP ( c-addr u --- op | -1 )
\ The last operation bearing the name, by t2_names' order (layout.py's
\ _inv: VAR-OPS's DOES> @ tail).
  2DUP OPS10-OF ?DUP IF SWAP DROP SWAP DROP EXIT THEN
  2DUP SPEC-OP DUP 0< 0= IF SWAP DROP SWAP DROP EXIT THEN DROP
  2DUP FIXED-OP DUP 0< 0= IF SWAP DROP SWAP DROP EXIT THEN DROP
  PRIM-OP ;
: CODE-OF ( c-addr u --- code -1 | 0 )
\ The last code bearing the name among those with a byte (INL-OPS's _code).
  2DUP OPS10-OF ?DUP IF BYTE-OF IF SWAP DROP SWAP DROP -1 EXIT THEN THEN
  2DUP SPEC-OP BYTE-OF IF SWAP DROP SWAP DROP -1 EXIT THEN
  2DUP FIXED-OP BYTE-OF IF SWAP DROP SWAP DROP -1 EXIT THEN
  PRIM-OP BYTE-OF ;
: FOLD-OP-OF ( c-addr u --- op | -1 )
\ The fold-set primitive's folded opcode (name;EXIT), if it is in the set.
  G-FOLDS LIST-INDEX DUP 0< IF EXIT THEN FOLD-BASE + ;
: PAIR-OP-OF ( c-addr1 u1 c-addr2 u2 --- op | -1 )
\ The fused pair "first second"'s opcode, if the design has it.
  G-SUPERS LIST-COUNT 3 / 0 ?DO
    2OVER I 3 * G-SUPERS LIST-TOKEN COMPARE 0= IF
      2DUP I 3 * 1+ G-SUPERS LIST-TOKEN COMPARE 0= IF
        2DROP 2DROP I 3 * 2 + G-SUPERS LIST-TOKEN TOKEN>N UNLOOP EXIT
      THEN
    THEN
  LOOP 2DROP 2DROP -1 ;
: VAR-OPS! ( --- )
\ vf, vs, @ and ! (all four or none - the fusion off), VARSLOT, SCALE 0;
\ the tag; DOES> @'s tail - R>, @;EXIT, the pair R> @, in one-byte codes -
\ and which of the three the design has.
  S" VAR-OPS" T-SHADOW 0= IF EXIT THEN @ >BODY-T >R
  4 SPEC? G-VARSLOT AND IF
    99 100 S" @" PRIM-OP S" !" PRIM-OP
    G-TAG2 IF
      >R >R >R T2C R> T2C R> T2C R> T2C
      2OVER 2OVER * * * 0= IF 2DROP 2DROP 0 0 0 0 THEN
    ELSE
      DUP 255 > IF DROP 125 THEN >R DUP 255 > IF DROP 125 THEN R>
    THEN
  ELSE 0 0 0 0 THEN
  R@ 3 + C!-T R@ 2 + C!-T R@ 1+ C!-T R@ C!-T
  G-VARSLOT IF 1 ELSE 0 THEN R@ 4 + C!-T  0 R@ 5 + C!-T
  G-TAG2 IF 1 ELSE 0 THEN R@ 6 + C!-T  0 R@ 7 + C!-T
  0 R@ 11 + C!-T
  4 SPEC? G-VARSLOT AND IF
    S" R>" LAST-OP BYTE-OF IF R@ 8 + C!-T R@ 11 + DUP C@-T 1 OR SWAP C!-T THEN
    S" @" FOLD-OP-OF BYTE-OF IF R@ 9 + C!-T R@ 11 + DUP C@-T 2 OR SWAP C!-T THEN
    S" R>" S" @" PAIR-OP-OF BYTE-OF IF R@ 10 + C!-T R@ 11 + DUP C@-T 4 OR SWAP C!-T THEN
  THEN
  R> DROP ;

\ INL-OPS: two bits a code, the length with its operand of what code
\ compiled at run time may copy for a call - layout.py's whitelist of the
\ operations that cannot tell where they sit; which codes are folds; the
\ JIT's code and header; the folds and their plain forms.
: INL-PURE ( --- c-addr u )
  S" NOOP DROP DUP SWAP ROT OVER C@ @ C! ! AND OR XOR = U< < + NEGATE LSHIFT RSHIFT UM* UM/MOD D+ SP@ 0= - <> 0< > 2DUP 2DROP CHAR+ 1+ CELL+ CELLS 1- INVERT COUNT ALIGNED lit0 lit1 litm1 +! ?DUP 2@ 2! FILL CMOVE " ;
: INL-OPND ( --- c-addr u ) S" LIT8 2 LIT 3 ADDI 2 EQI 2 SWAP+I 2 DUP+I 2 DUP<I 2 " ;
: PURE? ( c-addr u --- f ) INL-PURE LIST-INDEX 0< 0= ;
: ILEN ( c-addr u --- n )
  2DUP PURE? IF 2DROP 1 EXIT THEN INL-OPND LIST-VALUE 0 MAX ;
CREATE INL-BITS 256 ALLOT  VARIABLE IA
: BIT! ( n op --- ) BYTE-OF IF INL-BITS + C! ELSE DROP THEN ;
CREATE NBUF 32 ALLOT                              \ a fold's name: name;EXIT
: FOLD-NAME ( c-addr u --- c-addr' u' )
  DUP >R NBUF SWAP CMOVE S" ;EXIT" NBUF R@ + SWAP CMOVE NBUF R> 5 + ;
CREATE FP 26 20 * ALLOT  VARIABLE #FP          \ the folds: [name 16][u][fold code][plain code]
: FP# ( i --- addr ) 20 * FP + ;
: FP+ ( c-addr u fold-code plain-code --- )
  #FP @ FP# >R R@ 19 + C! R@ 18 + C! DUP R@ 16 + C! R> SWAP CMOVE 1 #FP +! ;
: FP-NAME ( i --- c-addr u ) FP# DUP 16 + C@ ;
CREATE FP-T 20 ALLOT
: FP-SORT ( --- )
\ By the fold's name, as Python's sorted() orders strings.
  #FP @ 2 < IF EXIT THEN
  #FP @ 1 DO
    I BEGIN DUP 0> WHILE
      DUP 1- FP-NAME 2 PICK FP-NAME COMPARE 0> 0= IF DROP 0 ELSE
        DUP FP# FP-T 20 CMOVE DUP 1- FP# OVER FP# 20 CMOVE FP-T OVER 1- FP# 20 CMOVE 1-
      THEN
    REPEAT DROP
  LOOP ;
: FOLD-CAND ( c-fold u-fold c-plain u-plain fold-op --- )
\ A fold and its plain form: kept if both have a code and the plain form
\ a length.
  BYTE-OF 0= IF 2DROP 2DROP EXIT THEN >R
  2DUP ILEN 0= IF 2DROP 2DROP R> DROP EXIT THEN
  CODE-OF 0= IF 2DROP R> DROP EXIT THEN          ( c-fold u-fold plain-code )
  OVER 16 > ABORT" cross: INL-OPS: a fold's name too long"
  R> SWAP FP+ ;
: INL-BITS! ( --- )
  INL-BITS 256 0 FILL
  INL-PURE LIST-COUNT 0 ?DO I INL-PURE LIST-TOKEN 2DUP ILEN ROT ROT PRIM-OP BIT! LOOP
  INL-OPND LIST-COUNT 2 / 0 ?DO I 2 * INL-OPND LIST-TOKEN 2DUP ILEN ROT ROT PRIM-OP BIT! LOOP
  0 68 BIT!  0 69 BIT!  0 70 BIT!  2 71 BIT!  0 72 BIT!  0 124 BIT!
  G-SPEC IF
    1 96 BIT! 1 97 BIT! 1 98 BIT!  105 99 DO 0 I BIT! LOOP
    TINY-SET LIST-COUNT 0 ?DO I TINY-SET LIST-TOKEN ILEN I TINY-BASE + BIT! LOOP
    2 120 BIT! 0 121 BIT! 2 122 BIT! 0 123 BIT!
  THEN
  G-FOLDS LIST-COUNT 0 ?DO 0 I FOLD-BASE + BIT! LOOP
  G-SUPERS LIST-COUNT 3 / 0 ?DO
    I 3 * G-SUPERS LIST-TOKEN PURE? I 3 * 1+ G-SUPERS LIST-TOKEN PURE? AND 1 AND
    I 3 * 2 + G-SUPERS LIST-TOKEN TOKEN>N BIT!
  LOOP
  G-OPS10 LIST-COUNT 2 / 0 ?DO
    I 2 * G-OPS10 LIST-TOKEN ILEN I 2 * 1+ G-OPS10 LIST-TOKEN TOKEN>N BIT!
  LOOP
  G-TAG2 G-JIT AND IF 0 65533 BIT! THEN ;
: INL-OPS! ( --- )
\ (The table's address in a variable: R@ inside DO ... LOOP is the loop's.)
  S" INL-OPS" T-SHADOW 0= IF EXIT THEN @ >BODY-T IA !
  INL-BITS!
  64 0 DO 0 4 0 DO J 4 * I + INL-BITS + C@ I 2* LSHIFT OR LOOP IA @ I + C!-T LOOP
  0 #FP !
  G-FOLDS LIST-COUNT 0 ?DO I G-FOLDS LIST-TOKEN 2DUP FOLD-NAME 2SWAP I FOLD-BASE + FOLD-CAND LOOP
  S" LIT8X" S" LIT8" 72 FOLD-CAND
  G-SPEC IF S" ADDIX" S" ADDI" 121 FOLD-CAND  S" EQIX" S" EQI" 123 FOLD-CAND THEN
  FP-SORT
  96 64 DO 0 IA @ I + C!-T LOOP
  #FP @ 0 ?DO
    I FP# 18 + C@ DUP 3 RSHIFT 64 + IA @ + DUP C@-T ROT 7 AND 1 SWAP LSHIFT OR SWAP C!-T
    I FP# 18 + C@ IA @ 99 + I 2* + C!-T  I FP# 19 + C@ IA @ 100 + I 2* + C!-T
  LOOP
  G-TAG2 G-JIT AND T2JIT @ 0< 0= AND IF T2JIT @ X-JITDEAD IF 1 ELSE 5 THEN ELSE 0 0 THEN IA @ 97 + C!-T IA @ 96 + C!-T
  #FP @ IA @ 98 + C!-T ;

\ PART 9: THE IMAGE FILE (engine/vm-lab.c, load_image): the magic, the
\ thread heads (one empty one, the design's thin header), no DOES> tails,
\ an empty locals block if the engine has the specialisations, THROW's
\ body, then the image.
CREATE MAGIC-CV8 67 C, 86 C, 56 C, 48 C, 8 C, 0 C, 1 C, 0 C,
CREATE CBUF 8 ALLOT
: CELL-OUT ( x fid --- ) >R CBUF ! CBUF TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ R> WRITE-FILE ABORT" cross: can't write" ;
VARIABLE FID-OUT
: SAVE-IMAGE-CV8 ( "name" --- )
\ (The file id in a variable: R@ inside DO ... LOOP is the loop's.)
  TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ MAGIC-CV8 4 + C!
  G-MAGIC5 MAGIC-CV8 5 + C!
  G-FEATURES #HOTS @ 0= IF 32 INVERT AND THEN MAGIC-CV8 7 + C!   \ one-byte calls: their table
  BL WORD COUNT W/O BIN CREATE-FILE ABORT" cross: can't create the image" FID-OUT !
  MAGIC-CV8 8 FID-OUT @ WRITE-FILE ABORT" cross: can't write"
  G-THIN-HEADER IF 1 FID-OUT @ CELL-OUT 0 FID-OUT @ CELL-OUT ELSE
    #TTHREADS FID-OUT @ CELL-OUT
    #TTHREADS 0 DO I CELLS TTHREADS + @ FID-OUT @ CELL-OUT LOOP
  THEN
  0 FID-OUT @ CELL-OUT
  G-ENGINE-SPEC IF 5 0 DO 0 FID-OUT @ CELL-OUT LOOP THEN
  S" THROW" T-SHADOW 0= ABORT" cross: no THROW" @ FID-OUT @ CELL-OUT
  #HOTS @ IF
    #HOTS @ CBUF C! CBUF 1 FID-OUT @ WRITE-FILE ABORT" cross: can't write"
    #HOTS @ 0 DO
      I CELLS HOTS + @ CELLS ORD-SH + @ @ DUP 65536 < 0= ABORT" cross: a one-byte call's target beyond 64 KB"
      CBUF ! CBUF 2 FID-OUT @ WRITE-FILE ABORT" cross: can't write"
    LOOP
  THEN
  IMAGE THERE FID-OUT @ WRITE-FILE ABORT" cross: can't write"
  FID-OUT @ CLOSE-FILE ABORT" cross: can't close" ;

\ The JIT's view of the image (the JIT designs' src/jit.c: Iteration 489's
\ jit_wends, 485-488's JIT_W_ offsets; tools/layout.py's _wends, _woff).
\ An image word the JIT reaches without the JIT's header ends where its
\ table says - every code word's body, start and end as image offsets,
\ the end where the next word's bytes begin - and (S"), (."), TYPE,
\ (ABORT") and the cold words EXECUTE's helper calls are known by their
\ offsets: this image's layout, built into the engine that runs it. They
\ go to cv8-self-jit.h, in vm-jit-ops.h's lines (tools/selfhost-check.sh
\ puts them in the design's for the engine it builds for the image).
CREATE JW-S #ORD-MAX CELLS ALLOT  VARIABLE #JW-S     \ the code words' bodies
CREATE JW-I #ORD-MAX CELLS ALLOT  VARIABLE #JW-I     \ where each word's bytes begin
VARIABLE FID-J
CREATE NM-SQ 4 C, 40 C, 83 C, 34 C, 41 C,            \ (S")
CREATE NM-DQ 4 C, 40 C, 46 C, 34 C, 41 C,            \ (.")
CREATE NM-AQ 8 C, 40 C, 65 C, 66 C, 79 C, 82 C, 84 C, 34 C, 41 C,   \ (ABORT")
: COLD-NAMES ( --- c-addr u ) S" EMIT TYPE CR SPACE SPACES . U. .R ABORT THROW KEY ACCEPT " ;
: LIVE? ( shadow --- f ) ORD DEAD + C@ 0= ;
: ITEM-START ( shadow --- t-addr )
\ A word's first byte: its link's - the link's length, less one, in the
\ top two bits of the byte before the count - or, with no header, its body's.
  DUP 3 CELLS + @ ?DUP IF SWAP DROP DUP 1- C@-T DUP 224 U< G-CHAINORDER 0= OR IF 6 RSHIFT 1+ ELSE DROP 3 THEN - ELSE @ THEN ;
\ 736: chainorder's forward link, the tag E0-FF, three bytes (it read four: the word before it a byte short, and
\ the JIT translated it so - small-jit's self-built image crashed in cross's own run).
: JW-ROW? ( shadow --- shadow f )
\ 723: with jitdead and not --jitx, the JIT-headed words' rows alone (layout.py's rows_).
  X-JITDEAD X-JITX 0= AND IF DUP @ JD-INDEX 0< 0= ELSE -1 THEN ;
: JW-COLLECT ( --- )
  0 #JW-S ! 0 #JW-I !
  #SHADOWS @ 0 ?DO
    I CELLS ORD-SH + @ DUP LIVE? IF
      DUP ITEM-START #JW-I @ CELLS JW-I + ! 1 #JW-I +!
      DUP CELL+ @ K-DATA = 0= IF JW-ROW? IF DUP @ #JW-S @ CELLS JW-S + ! 1 #JW-S +! THEN THEN
    THEN DROP
  LOOP
  X-JITDEAD IF #JD @ 0 ?DO 0 #JW-S @ 0 ?DO I CELLS JW-S + @ J CELLS JD-AT + @ = OR LOOP   \ an X and its X8: one body
    0= ABORT" cross: a JIT-headed body not among the words (jitdead)" LOOP THEN ;
: JW-END ( s --- e )
\ The least first byte above s, or the image's end - less jitdead's pad (723: layout.py's rows_ end before it).
  DUP THERE #JW-I @ 0 ?DO
    I CELLS JW-I + @ >R  OVER R@ < R@ 2 PICK < AND IF DROP R@ THEN R> DROP
  LOOP SWAP DROP  SWAP JD-INDEX DUP 0< IF DROP ELSE JD-PAD + C@ - THEN ;
: JW-NEXT ( last --- s | 0 )
\ The least body above last (a body is never at 0, a header is).
  0 #JW-S @ 0 ?DO
    I CELLS JW-S + @
    DUP 3 PICK > IF OVER 0= OVER 3 PICK < OR IF SWAP THEN THEN DROP
  LOOP SWAP DROP ;
: J-TYPE ( c-addr u --- ) FID-J @ WRITE-FILE ABORT" cross: can't write" ;
: J-NUM ( n --- ) DUP ABS 0 <# #S ROT SIGN #> J-TYPE ;
: J-CR ( --- ) 10 CBUF C! CBUF 1 J-TYPE ;
: J-OFF ( c-addr u --- t-addr | -1 )
\ The first live word of the name (layout.py's _woff): its body.
  #SHADOWS @ 0 ?DO
    I CELLS ORD-SH + @ DUP LIVE? IF
      DUP SH-NAME 4 PICK 4 PICK COMPARE 0= IF @ >R 2DROP R> UNLOOP EXIT THEN
    THEN DROP
  LOOP 2DROP -1 ;
: JW-MAX ( --- e )
\ The last body's end - the table's largest number (bodies do not overlap).
  0 BEGIN DUP JW-NEXT ?DUP WHILE SWAP DROP REPEAT DUP IF JW-END THEN ;
: SAVE-JIT-LAYOUT ( "name" --- )
  BL WORD COUNT G-JIT 0= IF 2DROP EXIT THEN
  W/O CREATE-FILE ABORT" cross: can't create the JIT's layout" FID-J !
  JW-COLLECT
  S" #define JIT_NWENDS " J-TYPE 0 0 BEGIN JW-NEXT ?DUP WHILE SWAP 1+ SWAP REPEAT J-NUM J-CR
  \ Iteration 710 (tools/layout.py's, wends16): two bytes a number where every end is under 64 KB
  JW-MAX 65536 < IF S" static const unsigned short jit_wends[][2] = {" ELSE S" static const unsigned int jit_wends[][2] = {" THEN J-TYPE
  0 0 BEGIN JW-NEXT ?DUP WHILE
    SWAP IF S" , " J-TYPE THEN
    S" {" J-TYPE DUP J-NUM S" , " J-TYPE DUP JW-END J-NUM S" }" J-TYPE
    -1 SWAP
  REPEAT DROP
  S" };" J-TYPE J-CR
  X-JITDEAD IF S" #define JITN_CODE " J-TYPE T2JITN @ DUP 0< ABORT" cross: no JITN code in the map" J-NUM J-CR THEN
  S" #define JIT_W_SQ " J-TYPE NM-SQ COUNT J-OFF J-NUM J-CR
  S" #define JIT_W_DQ " J-TYPE NM-DQ COUNT J-OFF J-NUM J-CR
  S" #define JIT_W_TYPE " J-TYPE S" TYPE" J-OFF J-NUM J-CR
  S" #define JIT_W_AQ " J-TYPE NM-AQ COUNT J-OFF J-NUM J-CR
  S" #define JIT_W_COLD " J-TYPE
  COLD-NAMES LIST-COUNT 0 ?DO
    I IF S" , " J-TYPE THEN I COLD-NAMES LIST-TOKEN J-OFF J-NUM
  LOOP J-CR
  FID-J @ CLOSE-FILE ABORT" cross: can't close" ;

: DP-END ( --- t-addr ) G-BSS IF BSS-PLACE ELSE THERE THEN ;

\ PART 10: THE PASSES - THE KERNEL, THE OVERLAYS, THE IMAGE.

: RESET ( --- )
\ Everything a pass builds, back to nothing: the image, its dictionary,
\ the shadows (TARGET's threads emptied), the pending calls and tables.
\ What the pass before found - the dead words, the one-byte calls, NEAR
\ - and the sources' pre-scan stay.
  IMAGE IMAGE_SIZE 0 FILL  0 DP-T !  0 TLINK !
  TTHREADS #TTHREADS CELLS 0 FILL
  TARGET-WID DUP @ 1+ 1 ?DO 0 OVER I CELLS + ! LOOP DROP
  0 STATE-T !  0 NEXT-OP !  0 NEXT-ESC !  FOLDMAP 128 0 FILL  SPECIAL-OPS 8 CELLS -1 FILL
  X8-SEEN 128 0 FILL  RB-RESET  FWD-RESET  -1 PAIRS-OPEN !  0 #PAIRS !
  0 #INLS !  0 #BSS !  0 ALLOT-HOOK !  0 #SHADOWS !  0 LAST-SHADOW !
  REFD #ORD-MAX 0 FILL  FREE# #ORD-MAX CELLS 0 FILL  ALL# #ORD-MAX CELLS 0 FILL
  0 #OPS !  0 HEADERLESS !  0 IN-KERNEL !  0 DEAD-NOW !
  0 #FWDP !  0 HS-ON !  0 HS-STORE !  0 HS-FINAL !  FAC-RESET  0 #JD !
  ONCE-SEEN 32 0 FILL  0 #HDR !  0 #CO-FWD ! ;   \ 736

: BUILD ( --- )
  RESET
  -1 IN-KERNEL ! S" kernel.4" INCLUDED 0 IN-KERNEL !
  XINCLUDE-OVERLAYS
  LAY-BODIES CHECK-PLACED FWDP-PATCH RESOLVE-FORWARDS RESOLVE-REBINDS
  G-CHAINORDER CO-WALK @ AND IF CO-FINISH THEN       \ 736: chainorder's forward links and heads
  S" FORTH-WORDLIST" TXT >BODY-T PUBLISH-WORDLIST
  DP-END S" DP" TXT >BODY-T !-T
\ The dictionary's room from START: the CV8 engines keep the stacks apart, in
\ 256 MB of their own (engine/vm-lab.c's MEMMAX; kernel.4's DICT-MAX, which the
\ translator wrote too - tools/layout.py, Iteration 184).
  268435456 S" DICT-MAX" TXT >BODY-T !-T
  FOLD-OPS! FOLD-TABLE! SUPER-TABLE! IMM-OPS! LOOPTAB! VAR-OPS! INL-OPS! ;

\ After a pass: the dead words (to leave out of the next), the one-byte
\ calls' targets (for the next) - each the same as the pass before found,
\ once that pass had them to go by.
: SHADOWED? ( k --- f ) CELLS ORD-SH + @ DUP SH-NAME T-SHADOW IF <> ELSE DROP 0 THEN ;
CREATE DEAD2 #ORD-MAX ALLOT  VARIABLE #DEAD 0 #DEAD !
: FIND-DEAD ( --- )
  DEAD2 #ORD-MAX 0 FILL 0 #DEAD !
  #SHADOWS @ 0 ?DO
    I REFD + C@ 0= IF I CELLS ORD-SH + @ CELL+ @ K-DATA = 0= IF
      I SHADOWED? IF 1 I DEAD2 + C! 1 #DEAD +! THEN
    THEN THEN
  LOOP
  PASS @ 1 > IF DEAD #ORD-MAX DEAD2 #ORD-MAX COMPARE ABORT" cross: the dead words moved between passes" THEN
  DEAD2 DEAD #ORD-MAX CMOVE ;

: FOLD-COUNTS ( --- )
\ The sites of calls chained to a FORWARD or a rebound name, given to the
\ word they reached.
  FWD-LIST @ BEGIN ?DUP WHILE
    DUP 3 CELLS + @ IF
      DUP FWD-SHADOW DUP 0= ABORT" cross: a forward never resolved" ORD CELLS >R
      DUP 2 CELLS + @ R@ FREE# + +!  DUP 3 CELLS + @ R> ALL# + +!
    THEN @
  REPEAT
  #RBS @ 0 ?DO                       \ (no >R here: I would read it)
    I RB# DUP 4 CELLS + @ IF
      DUP RB-SHADOW ORD CELLS                      ( rec off )
      OVER 3 CELLS + @ OVER FREE# + +!
      SWAP 4 CELLS + @ SWAP ALL# + +!
    ELSE DROP THEN
  LOOP ;
: BETTER? ( k1 k2 --- f )
\ k1 ranks before k2: more free sites, then more sites, then defined first
\ (layout.py's order, its old address in the ordinal's place).
  OVER CELLS FREE# + @ OVER CELLS FREE# + @ 2DUP <> IF > >R 2DROP R> EXIT THEN 2DROP
  OVER CELLS ALL# + @ OVER CELLS ALL# + @ 2DUP <> IF > >R 2DROP R> EXIT THEN 2DROP
  < ;
CREATE CHOSEN #ORD-MAX ALLOT
CREATE NEWHOTS 32 CELLS ALLOT  VARIABLE #NEWHOTS
: PICK-HOT ( --- k | -1 )
\ The best target not chosen yet with three free sites - two would only
\ pay for its entry in the table.
  -1 #SHADOWS @ 0 ?DO
    I CHOSEN + C@ 0= I CELLS FREE# + @ 3 < 0= AND IF
      DUP 0< IF DROP I ELSE I OVER BETTER? IF DROP I THEN THEN
    THEN
  LOOP ;
: SET-HOT-RECORDS ( --- )
\ What a pending call to a FORWARD or a rebound name is in the next pass.
  FWD-LIST @ BEGIN ?DUP WHILE DUP FWD-SHADOW ?DUP IF ORD HOT-CODE ELSE 0 THEN OVER 4 CELLS + ! @ REPEAT
  #RBS @ 0 ?DO I RB# DUP @ OVER CELL+ @ T-SHADOW IF ORD HOT-CODE ELSE 0 THEN SWAP 5 CELLS + ! LOOP ;
: FIND-HOT ( --- )
  FOLD-COUNTS
  CHOSEN #ORD-MAX 0 FILL 0 #NEWHOTS !
  G-HOTCALLS 32 MIN 0 ?DO
    PICK-HOT DUP 0< IF DROP ELSE
      1 OVER CHOSEN + C!  #NEWHOTS @ CELLS NEWHOTS + !  1 #NEWHOTS +!
    THEN
  LOOP
  PASS @ 2 > IF
    #NEWHOTS @ #HOTS @ <> ABORT" cross: the one-byte calls moved between passes"
    NEWHOTS #HOTS @ CELLS HOTS #HOTS @ CELLS COMPARE ABORT" cross: the one-byte calls moved between passes"
  THEN
  NEWHOTS HOTS 32 CELLS CMOVE #NEWHOTS @ #HOTS !
  SET-HOT-RECORDS ;

: REPORT ( --- )
  S" cross-cv8: pass " TYPE PASS @ . S" - " TYPE THERE . S" bytes, " TYPE
  #DEAD @ . S" dead words out, " TYPE #HOTS @ . S" one-byte calls" TYPE CR ;

: PASSES ( --- )
  SCAN-SOURCES
  1 PASS ! BUILD FIND-DEAD THERE 16384 < NEAR ! REPORT
  2 PASS ! -1 COUNTING ! BUILD FIND-DEAD FIND-HOT REPORT
  G-CHAINORDER IF CO-WALK! -1 CO-WALK ! THEN          \ 736: the third pass lays the walk
  FAC-SEARCH
  3 PASS ! BUILD FIND-DEAD FIND-HOT REPORT ;

PASSES
SAVE-IMAGE-CV8 cv8-self.img
SAVE-JIT-LAYOUT cv8-self-jit.h
BYE
